(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-8"] = {"468305101":[["Mercenary A","This place is so hard to find! It's hidden so well, there must be a lot of good stuff inside!"],["Mercenary B","Obviously! Why else would we bust our asses coming all the way out here if there wasn't something good?"],["","Two mercenaries whisper to each other."],["","They huddled together with other companions in an inconspicuous mine pit, covered by a cloth meant to deceive the monitors."],["","The edge of the cloth was propped up, creating a narrow slit, and occasionally a few telescopes would poke through the gap, carefully observing the distant old buildings."],["Mercenary A","I can't believe Harpy uses this dump as a warehouse. The biggest trade guild on Milkhama, hiding stock in a place like this... who would buy that—ah!"],["","The mercenary was slapped. The one who struck him was scanning the warehouse through binoculars, never sparing him a glance, yet the blow landed squarely on his face."],["Douglas","Enough talk. Stay sharp. This is a critical moment, don't screw it up!"],["Mercenary A","Y-yes, boss."],["","The crowd surged, and a small group squeezed to Douglas's side from the outskirts."],["Jon","Depot security situation detected, boss. Just like the intel, they've only stationed a small group there, with fixed shift times, not hard to slip past."],["Rena","There are a total of sixteen camera points. If we break in from Zone U according to the plan... I can handle the related surveillance."],["Douglas","Good job, then let's go with the original plan. Team one will create some noise to distract them, and the rest will follow me."],["","The group instinctively turned toward the rear of the formation, where a cluster of mercenaries stood wrapped tight. Ever since the ambush began, they had lingered there like ghosts, silent and unmoving."],["","Douglas had been aligned with the Predators for some time, yet he still hadn't fully grown used to operating alongside these masked figures—perhaps the truly unrestrained strong are feared no matter where they stand."],["Predator Mercenary","Understood, looking forward to our cooperation."],["","After saying this, he made a gesture and left the mine with a group of people wrapped up just like him."],["Douglas","Ahem—alright, check your equipment. We move out in two minutes!"],["Rena","Wait a minute, boss."],["Douglas","Tsk! What else?"],["Rena","I want to confirm with you again, this operation..."],["Jon","Rena."],["","Jon tugged Rena's arm to say something, but was stopped short by Rena's gaze."],["Rena","Boss, maybe we should think this through one last time. Harpy's one of the island's biggest middle powers, and they stay on good terms with most merc crews. Are we really going to piss them off over a bit of pocket change?"],["Douglas","Heh, pocket change? You're still too naive, Rena."],["","Douglas pointed at the distant warehouse clusters with a disdainful smile."],["Douglas","I've got intel—Harpy has dozens of warehouses like this across Milkhama. The stockpiles they've been hoarding lately are worth at least hundreds of millions. And you call that pocket change?"],["Rena","Boss... you know what I'm worried about."],["Douglas","Then let me tell you this—you're doing something unnecessary. Rena, Milkhama is a mess right now. Fighting could break out at any moment, and this isn't the kind of small skirmish you used to deal with…"],["Douglas","All factions will get involved, and Milkhama will slowly turn into a vortex. Either you get out early, or you dig your roots deep, otherwise you'll eventually be torn apart by that vortex."],["Rena","......"],["","Rena looked troubled, seemingly caught in quite a dilemma."],["Douglas","When the real fight starts, it won't be easy for Harpy to maintain true neutrality. Besides, what do they mean by stockpiling supplies at this time? They might have gotten some news and are preparing to make a big profit!"],["Douglas","I, Douglas, cannot fall behind. In any case, today's job must be done, even if you want to leave, finish the task first, or else... you know how I treat those who don't listen."],["","Douglas gave Rena a smile that didn't reach his eyes, patted her shoulder, and then withdrew from the mine with his group of underlings."],["","Jon and Rena stayed in place, watching him leave. After Douglas's distant silhouette disappeared, Rena's shoulders instantly slumped."],["Jon","Don't take it to heart, he's always been like that."],["Rena","Sigh... Jon, I just hope we can stay here a little longer this time... Even though Douglas isn't easy to get along with as the boss."],["Jon","Haha, I understand, Rena, but sometimes, sometimes we have to accept the reality."],["Rena","Alright... Maybe I had too many expectations."],["Jon","Douglas is ruthless and unpredictable, so it's best to avoid provoking him. If things go south in the end... at least we can still protect ourselves."],["","Jon chuckled, gave Rena a firm pat on the back, and then ran ahead. Rena took a deep breath to steady herself and quickly followed his lead."],["","Douglas led his men to crowd at the edge of the mine. A minute later, the sound of an explosion came from afar, and Douglas quickly raised his binoculars, indeed seeing a squad of mechs winding out from the warehouse."],["Douglas","They fell for it! Rena, is everything set on your end?"],["Rena","The surveillance footage has been switched. Proceeding along the planned route will be fine."],["Douglas","Nice! Keep your skin tight and run, I'll shoot the first one who falls behind!"],["","Douglas charged ahead with excitement, and the group moved swiftly, closing in on Zone U—the warehouse's weakest point of defense."],["","They clearly hadn't expected an intrusion at this moment—the guards were caught completely off guard when the mercenaries stormed in."],["","However, by the time they regain their senses and prepare to sound the alarm, the mercenaries have already pulled the trigger on them. After a few faint gunshots, several bodies lay sprawled on the ground."],["Rena","I have temporarily closed off this area, sending out safety simulation signals every ten minutes. As long as we don't make too much noise, we shouldn't be discovered."],["Rena","Guard rotations run every thirty minutes. A direct confrontation would be troublesome—move fast."],["Douglas","You all hear that? Move, move, move! Check what's valuable—take everything and haul it out!"],["Douglas","Come with me, a few of you. Let's bring the STs over!"],["","The mercenaries quickly got into position, dispersing into the gaps between the shelves, tapping and knocking along the way, their gaze so intense it seemed to burn holes into the items on the shelves."],["","Rena looked around. The less than hundred-square-meter open space was filled with shelves, and stacks of heavy wooden boxes piled up high beyond reach."],["","She took out her portable detector and pried open a nearby box, revealing black gun barrels that reflected a faint cold light."],["Jon","It's all hot weapons and ammo... Harpy is really stockpiling military supplies on a large scale. Could they have really heard some rumors?"],["Rena","......"],["","Rena silently looked down at the detector's screen. The layers of green lines maintained a regular frequency of undulation from left to right, except for one line that fluctuated somewhat abnormally."],["Rena","Strange..."],["Jon","What?"],["","Rena began to move around the warehouse, searching for the source of the anomaly."],["","After almost walking through the entire warehouse, Rena finally found several large boxes in a corner and quickly called Jon to help open them."],["Jon","These... are just ST Parts, what's so strange about them?"],["Rena","The detector shows... they are emitting some strange electromagnetic waves."],["Jon","Could it be the influence of Arashi Matter?"],["Rena","Maybe...? I'm not sure, I rarely see such irregular electrical signals on ST Parts, and the frequency is far lower than that of regular parts."],["Jon","Could this be new technology that Harpy got from somewhere? Preparing to bring some new shock to the battlefield...?"],["","The two exchanged a silent glance. Rena decisively put away the detector, adopting a \"let's get to work\" stance."],["Rena","Whatever, since we're already on this pirate ship, we might as well make the most of our efforts, right? Let's get these big guys out first and study them later."],["","Rena called over some more people, and they used rollers to move the boxes to the warehouse entrance, then had the STs grab them like loaves of bread and place them into the truck."],["Douglas","Hmm? Are there ST parts here?"],["Rena","Yes, but these parts might..."],["Douglas","Perfect, the new arm guards I replaced earlier just don't feel right. You, you, both of you come over and help me swap them out again—"],["Rena","They're quite different from regular parts."],["","Douglas has already opened the ST arm control interface, and two underlings are helping him replace the arm guards—clearly not intending to pay attention to Rena's long speech."],["Rena","...Eh."],["Jon","He even modified Kong just to keep his identity hidden for this operation—he's been grumbling about it for days. Now that we're almost done, it's normal he can't hold it in anymore."],["Jon","Alright, let's go see what else we can take with us."],["","The two of them walked together to the other side of the warehouse, completing the final stocktake of the remaining supplies."],["Rena","There's not much space left in the cargo hold. If we continue to fill it up, it might affect our speed... Should we change our retreat route?"],["Jon","No worries, the remaining goods can be transported by ST. As long as we leave before the next guard shift change, we won't be detected. Let me check how much time we have left..."],["","BANG—!!!"],["","Without warning, a thunderous crash of STs colliding erupted at the warehouse entrance. The ground shook for two full seconds, metal racks swayed violently, then collapsed in a clatter."],["","Rena and Jon exchange a startled glance and quickly rush out."],["Rena","What's going on?! Didn't I say not to make a big fuss?!"],["Mercenary B","Ugh—! Help! Help—!"],["Rena","Wh-What?!"],["","The scene before her shocked Rena, causing her to involuntarily step back two paces."],["","A massive shadow looms over her. Douglas grabs the cockpit of the nearby ST, as casually as an ordinary person would pick up a crab."],["Mercenary B","Help! Help! Boss, don't kill me! Spare me, boss—!"],["Douglas","Shut up, fool! It wasn't me!"],["Douglas","The control module is not responding! What's going on?! This arm armor can't connect to the control center! Where's Rena—?!"],["","Douglas locked Rena's position on the display screen."],["Douglas","Ah! You're here—quick, think of something and figure out what's going on!"],["","As soon as Douglas finished speaking, Kong's right arm reached out uncontrollably towards Rena."],["","Jon immediately rushed forward and tackled her to the ground. The detector on Rena was thrown out, and the lines on it had already turned into abstract art."],["","Rena shivered, and an uncontrollable concept popped into her mind."],["Rena","It's... it's been activated!"],["Jon","Activated?! What on earth is this thing?!"],["Rena","I—I don't know! J-just get those gauntlets off first! If this keeps up, the noise it's making will ruin everything we've done!"],["Jon","No, we can't get close to it, unless..."],["Douglas","Damn it! Grab the rockets! Blast it down with the rockets!"],["Douglas","You guys move the cargo that can be transported first! Leave a few people behind to smash it with rockets! Get moving now!"],["Jon","I've got this!"],["","Jon rolled into cover, quickly grabbing a rocket gunport from the box and loading ammo. Rena had just found cover when he was already adjusting the angle adjustment, moving with incredible speed—"],["","Looks like they've been wanting to blast Douglas for quite some time."],["Jon","Take cover, and—fire!"],["","With a sharp whistling screech, a rocket detonated at Kong's right-arm joint, bursting into thick black smoke as faint sparks crackled—this shot should have severed the connected power lines."],["Jon","We did it! Quick! Pull the right arm off now!"],["Rena","No! Wait! Something's not right..."],["","As the black smoke dissipates, Kong's right arm bends at an extremely unnatural angle, with the metal casing near the connection turning into a dark liquid resembling lava."],["","It generates a web-like black membrane at the break between the body and arm, and as the residual current flickers, the black membrane suddenly contracts, reattaching the mechanical arm to the body."],["Douglas","What's going on?! The connector indicates it hasn't detached from the ST at all?!"],["Rena","It, it it it..."],["","Everything before her left Rena speechless. Clearly, this was beyond her understanding. An arm that was severed can automatically reconnect?"],["","At this moment, the detector in her hand vibrated slightly. When she held it up, the lines on the screen were no longer as chaotic as before."],["","After a few seconds of daze, a new hypothesis formed in her mind."],["Rena","Temperature! It's high temperature!"],["Jon","What? You thought of a way?"],["","Rena hurriedly pulled several rockets from a crate and handed them to Jon, while fumbling to load a rocket launcher herself."],["Rena","It's high temperature. High temperature can fully activate them—maybe firing a few more rounds and adjusting the electromagnetic wave frequency to match the ordinary parts should successfully connect them."],["Rena","The tools are crude, but the situation is urgent, so let's go with this for now!"],["Jon","Got it!"],["","Jon and Rena hoisted the rocket launchers onto their shoulders and fired four rounds in rapid succession."],["","Such close-range attack, the powerful impact forced Douglas to Pilot Kong to retreat a distance to buffer the pressure. Black smoke filled the air, and Kong's shadow was gradually engulfed into invisibility."],["Jon","...Did it work?"],["Douglas","......"],["Douglas","Connector, normal, control module... response normal—! Hahaha... hahahahaha!"],["","Douglas excitedly manipulated Kong, constantly changing its movements. The newly installed arm guards seemed to suit his taste."],["Jon","Phew… at least nothing major went wrong."],["Rena","No—too soon to celebrate. We just unloaded like that, unless Harpy's security are all deaf…"],["","Jon's expression changed."],["Jon","Quick, retreat!"],["Harpy Security","I've reached the outskirts of Zone U... Damn, there are signs of intrusion here."],["Harpy Employee","The enemy is clever, they modified the surveillance to bypass the defense system. I'll report immediately, stay safe during your operation."],["Harpy Security","Received."],["Harpy Security","Two teams follow me, the rest block the exit, don't let anyone out..."],["","The security officer was arranging tasks when suddenly a rumbling vibration came from the ground, and a squad of mech soldiers approached head-on—"],["Rena","Damn! It's Harpy's men!"],["Douglas","What are you afraid of? Taking care of these guys is easy! Get juiced and show them the strength of the Douglas Mercenary Team!"],["Harpy Security","Damn it... arrogant bastards... Go! Take them all down!"]],"468305301":[["Rena","This is bad! Their firepower is too strong—if this keeps up, our patched-together STs won't hold out!"],["Douglas","Forget about those guys! The cargo's already shipped, we need to get out of here quickly!"],["Jon","Let me cover you, aim for the gaps and get out of here!"],["Rena","Jon!"],["","As soon as the words were spoken, Jon piloted the ST into the hail of bullets. Rena intended to follow, but Douglas stopped her."],["Douglas","Forget about him, if you really care, you should be running now!"],["Rena","But..."],["Douglas","Our equipment is outside, can't you go out and come back for him?"],["","Rena was a bit anxious. Her peripheral vision suddenly caught sight of a squad of STs quickly approaching from a distance, and her worry turned to joy as she recognized their identity."],["Rena","Great, it's you guys!"],["Predator Mercenary","Why aren't you leaving? There's no time."],["Rena","Some people haven't evacuated yet, we need to go and get them!"],["Douglas","Didn't you hear?! There's no time left! We need to leave now! We've got the goods, just one last step left—"],["","Douglas has already turned to prepare for retreat, and Rena quickly rushed over to grab the arm armor of the ST."],["Rena","We have to go get them. Boss—if they're captured, who's to say they won't sell us out to save themselves?!"],["Douglas","You—!"],["","The Predator Mercenary glanced at the distant battlefield and then patted the ST beside Rena."],["Predator Mercenary","We can give it a try, you retreat first, Douglas."],["Douglas","Fine, do whatever you want!"],["Douglas","I'll send you the rendezvous coordinates. It's a secluded spot, perfect for splitting the loot."],["","Deep in the East Desert"],["???","Been a while, my friend. You look... haha, just like before."],["Gutzman","You too, Toman—still as sharp as ever."],["","The two laughed and exchanged a courteous hug."],["Toman","You're right on time. Mr. Henry is inside tidying up his new ride. I'll take you to meet him."],["","Toman leads Gutzman outside."],["","They walk around a private property deep in the East Desert. Tall and luxurious buildings surround an expensive artificial lake, while outside lies a sea of endless yellow sand."],["Gutzman","Mr. Henry still has such a flair. The last time we met... I remember it was at Burton Bay, on his newly built artificial island."],["Toman","Is that so? It must have been a memorable meeting then. Mr. Henry is quite an unconventional person. I've served many dignitaries, and his taste has always been surprising."],["Gutzman","It was indeed a pleasant surprise. Being willing to maintain a long-term collaboration with my newly established mercenary group requires a certain level of fearlessness."],["Toman","He enjoys seeking thrills—though you didn't disappoint him. Mr. Henry is very pleased with you and has praised your abilities more than once."],["Gutzman","Hahaha."],["","Gutzman smiled without responding. He turned his head to look at the shimmering lake under the corridor, lost in thought."],["","The recent jobs have somewhat exceeded their control capabilities, and the results were not quite Perfect. He was unsure if Henry's attitude would remain the same as before."],["","They quickly arrived at their destination. On the wide open space beside the lake, a towering giant ST was silently undergoing inspection and cleaning."],["","Gutzman looked at the ST, and at Henry, who was hanging in front of it, personally wiping it down. He stopped and gave Toman a puzzled look."],["Toman","Don't be surprised, Mr. Henry recently found the cockpit of his previous vehicle a bit cramped, so he specially ordered this Hades from Obsidian... It should keep him happy for a couple of days."],["Gutzman","I didn't expect Mr. Henry to bring this exclusive giant weapon back to light... You're doing better and better, Toman."],["Toman","Heh... Do you have something to ask him for help with today?"],["Gutzman","... The situation has been tense lately... I found a place that's very suitable for a base, highly concealed, and the military can't easily interfere..."],["","Gutzman paused, and Toman didn't respond, just gestured with his eyes for him to continue."],["Gutzman","But unfortunately, those Shadow guys clearly have the same idea as me."],["Toman","Oh... that's really unfortunate, my friend. I know the leader of the Shadow - Malcolm isn't that easy to deal with. The first thing you need to learn when dealing with him is to soften your knees..."],["","Toman patted Gutzman on the back, both regretful and approving."],["Toman","But I know you're as hard as steel all over!"],["Gutzman","Hehe..."],["","Gutzman shook his head slightly."],["Gutzman","The recent jobs have been quite difficult, and I've lost quite a few men... But as long as Mr. Henry takes action, Malcolm will have no choice but to kneel."],["Gutzman","I need some money to take him on, to make him fully understand how he should deal with me in the future."],["Toman","......"],["Toman","Hahaha, of course, that's why I have high hopes for you, my friend. I wish you all the best."],["","Toman bowed slightly, inviting Gutzman to go first. The two walked down together, and Henry saw them from high above, smiling and waving."],["Mr. Henry","What are you whispering about? You two have been standing there and not coming over."],["Toman","Just didn't want to disturb your leisurely time with your new ride—"],["Mr. Henry","Yes! You're right! Look—look at this guy, it's unbelievable, the bumpkins outside of Milkhama would never see this thing!"],["Toman","It is indeed astonishing and perfectly matches your status."],["","Henry laughed and gave Hades a couple of hearty slaps, then operated the pulley at his waist to slowly descend from the air."],["Mr. Henry","Haven't seen you for a while, I almost forgot what you look like."],["","Henry walked under the shade of the umbrella and poured himself a drink, while Toman and Gutzman exchanged a glance."],["Mr. Henry","I happen to have something I want to discuss with Gutzman, so your timing is perfect."],["","Henry threw himself onto the sofa, stretching out his limbs comfortably."],["Gutzman","It seems we understand each other."],["Mr. Henry","Haha, I want to give you some money."],["","Gutzman's eyes widened slightly, and his heart pounded with a heavy thud."],["","For a couple of seconds, he thought he was dreaming, dreaming that a genie had stolen the deepest thoughts of his heart, believing that with so many people in the world enjoying life every day, it was finally Gutzman's turn, the one who had always been unlucky—"],["","He was finally favored by fate for no apparent reason, even though the chosen representative, Henry, had a rather peculiar style... but who cares?"],["","Gutzman breathed a sigh of relief, feeling as if sturdy steel nails had been driven into the seams of his spine. He straightened his back and walked briskly towards Henry."],["Gutzman","Thank you for your trust, Mr. Henry. I think we can talk about the next job now."],["Mr. Henry","I'm going to give you some money, Gutzman, and then you can take it and get out."],["Toman","...?"],["","Toman quickly glanced between Gutzman and Henry, inexplicably starting to feel nervous. Henry's voice was loud enough for Gutzman to hear, but he still showed no reaction."],["Mr. Henry","You can leave now. My assistant will transfer the money to your account."],["Gutzman","Henry..."],["Mr. Henry","Oh, don't be like that, Gutzman. We worked so well together before... I admire you, truly. I see you as an incredibly sharp blade, my favorite in my collection."],["Mr. Henry","But I really don't like flawed items. You should understand me, right?"],["Toman","...... Haha, Mr. Henry, actually, all blades in this world need constant honing to become sharper..."],["Mr. Henry","Shallow, too shallow! Only things born with defects need constant polishing—perfect collections require no corrections!"],["Gutzman","......"],["Mr. Henry","Enough, we can't communicate on the same level."],["Mr. Henry","Take the severance pay and get out..."],["","Henry paused, seemingly feeling that he hadn't fully expressed his emotions, and thought for a few seconds."],["Mr. Henry","Or, you could use this money to polish yourself up, and I'll see what else you can do—ha! If I still remember you by then!"],["Gutzman","......"],["","Gutzman remained silent, expressionless. His gaze was fixed on Henry, watching as Henry casually finished his drink and then energetically sprang up from the couch, running towards his beloved Hades, muttering something under his breath."],["","Gutzman and Toman seemed like two transparent people, completely disappearing from his world."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Boss, how's it going?"],["Gutzman","......"],["","Gutzman didn't say a word."],["","He looked back into the distance, where the desert lake had shrunk to the size of a fingernail, light and airy, as if a very small force could blow it away."],["","But Gutzman understood that it would take a long journey to overturn it."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Wha-what's wrong, Boss? That lunatic doesn't want to pay?"],["Gutzman","Don't disturb me."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Yes! It's..."],["Gutzman","......"],["","The two remained silent for a long time."],["Gutzman Mercenary","B-boss, I don't dare disturb you, but there's something I need to report."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Malcolm has tied up three of our brothers again... He, he sent a video..."],["Gutzman","...What's in the video? Is he asking for ransom?"],["Gutzman Mercenary","He... he killed those three people, didn't ask for ransom."],["","What he wanted was a warning."],["","Guzman took a deep breath, then slowly let it out, pulling his gaze back from the distance as he turned to leave."],["Gutzman","Alright, tell the people below not to clash with Malcolm's men for now."],["Gutzman Mercenary","What? Are we going to make concessions?"],["","Gutzman's steps halted, and his followers instantly fell silent."],["Gutzman","I have other plans, just go and relay the message."],["","*beep-beep*"],["","He continued forward, and the communicator in his pocket suddenly rang... it was someone he truly didn't expect at this moment."],["Harpy Contact","Gutzman?"],["Gutzman","It's me."],["Gutzman","It's rare to receive communication from you. What's up?"],["Harpy Contact","Our warehouse was robbed recently, and we suffered significant losses. The thieves are likely from your circle, and the higher-ups want them captured alive to teach them a lesson."],["Gutzman","...Heh heh heh, what about the payment?"],["Harpy Contact","Eight figures."],["","Gutzman rubbed his face, and when he spoke again, his voice sounded much more relaxed."],["Gutzman","As expected of Harpy Commerce, they always make a grand entrance."],["Harpy Contact","Don't get too excited just yet. This bounty isn't exclusive to you—it's first come, first served. So, are you taking the job?"],["Gutzman","...If I told you that money is definitely going to be mine, would you believe me?"],["Harpy Contact","I believe you."],["Gutzman","Hahaha! This is great... Harpy Commerce."],["Harpy Contact","If there are no other questions, the necessary supplies and intel will be delivered to you soon, Gutzman. Don't let us down."]],"468309101":[["","Huff... hiss... huff... hiss... huff..."],["","Oxygen deprivation. Pain. Every breath feels like it's wrapped in burning coals."],["","Georgia's mind went completely blank, leaving only a thin line of white noise, pressed to its limit, echoing helplessly."],["","She suddenly bites her tongue, spitting out a mouthful of bloody foam."],["","She couldn't fall here—not like this. But compared to the damage dealt by her opponent, the self-inflicted pain felt no more than a mosquito bite."],["","Her consciousness begins to fade, almost drowning in the clamoring pain."],["???","72 minutes, Georgia. Is that really all you've got today?"],["","No, no..."],["???","…Sigh. Then this is where it ends."],["Georgia","No... No...!"],["","She heard a strange, hoarse voice coming from her throat, but her mind still couldn't generate any images."],["","The punch the instructor landed on her face was too fast and fierce to dodge, and she thought she might have a mild concussion."],["","She felt like vomiting."],["???","Swallow it, Georgia. You can't show a hint of weakness, or your opponent will snap your neck immediately."],["","Georgia heard approaching footsteps, and the instructor crouched beside her ear. She wanted to say she could still stand, but the next moment, she felt a strong pressure on her neck, as if trying to twist her throat."],["???","Just like this, Georgia..."],["Georgia","!?"],["","Her whole body was boiling, and the blood vessels in her brain seemed about to burst from the rushing blood."],["???","......"],["???","Maybe I shouldn't have come to you. There's someone better suited for this task..."],["","No, no...you..."],["Georgia","What the hell are you talking about?!"],["","Bang!"],["","Georgia suddenly opened her eyes. The scene before her was still a bit shaky. She barely pulled her thoughts from the memory and found her position."],["Audience Member A","Crocodile! Crocodile! Crocodile!"],["Audience Member B","There's your chance, Crocodile! Crush her—harder! Squeeze her brain out!"],["Audience Member A","Take back your crown! Crocodile!—Kill her!!"],["Georgia","*Spit!*"],["","Georgia spat out blood foam and clenched her teeth."],["","The bloody smell mixed with dust, the damp and musty odor accumulated in the arena that never sees daylight, and the filthy stench gathered by the crowd... Georgia felt genuinely nauseated."],["","She rolled her eyes, peering through a gap that was neither wide nor narrow at her opponent—the so-called \"Crocodile.\" They piloted a dark-green, cobbled-together mech, dual blades in hand, one of them nearly piercing her cockpit."],["","The STs provided by this underground ST arena are all junk, as thin as paper, and almost have no shock absorption. The vibrations transmitted during collisions can easily cause concussions or even internal injuries."],["","In the recent collision, Crocodile broke her pilot cabin, and the intense vibration caused her to briefly lose consciousness. Fortunately, even while unconscious, her hand tightly controlled the control stick."],["","Otherwise, she would have been split in half by Crocodile directly, instead of having the chance to engage in a technical competition with him and wait for the right moment."],["","Her heart was racing, which was not a good sign. Perhaps she couldn't wait any longer."],["Crocodile","I know you're waiting for my power engine to become overloaded. You're different from those fools who only come to die under my blade."],["Crocodile","You've been trained, and before going into battle, you must have seen how terrible the condition of these STs really is..."],["","Georgia heard the strained creaking of the arm guard, gradually losing the strength to stop the opponent's blade from slicing through the pilot cabin's shell. This outdated cobbled-together ST couldn't even keep its sensors consistently functional, so she could only rely on her experience to judge how long these parts could hold."],["Crocodile","But you and I are different."],["Crocodile","In the 'Underground Steam,' everyone knows my name—because everyone loves a winner… This is my honor, you little brat…"],["Crocodile","You have no idea how much time and money it took me to get this far, or how many times I've walked on the edge of death. You can't even imagine."],["Crocodile","Regret it, you shouldn't have come here to seize what doesn't belong to you!"],["","Crocodile strutted as he delivered his declaration. In his eyes, the fight was already over—once he slowly, deliberately sliced open that shell as thin as paper, the pressure alone would crush his opponent's resolve."],["","That's usually the case. amateur challengers rarely have the guts to risk their lives. Crocodile used to be a mercenary making a living in gunfire. He doesn't want to die, but he's not afraid of death either. With such decision, he remains unbroken in the \"Underground Steam\"."],["","Over the years, he has developed a unique competitive process. His goal is to create \"visually appealing sustained victories,\" so he pushes the battle to a stalemate, building suspense before delivering the final blow."],["","He also pays attention to controlling the number of kills, making the challengers feel that even if they lose, there is a high probability of surviving, which encourages them to persistently challenge him."],["","Although today's opponent made him nervous for a moment, fortunately, he has regained the initiative. As long as he applies verbal pressure, he should be able to force her to surrender soon."],["","—The opponent is a woman, so she is lucky because Crocodile does not kill women."],["Georgia","ESD-314, among all the armguards circulating in the black market, it has the lowest energy transfer loss efficiency, which is why your blade speed is so fast."],["Crocodile","...Seems like you know your stuff. That's right, you can't keep winning with just the scrap metal provided here, so I modified all the ST parts—"],["Crocodile","This also means the overload you've been waiting for will never come. Too bad you didn't realize this sooner."],["Georgia","No, it's just right now."],["Crocodile","What do you mean—ah!!"],["","Georgia suddenly completely gave up resistance and even actively approached the Crocodile, who was so shocked that he instinctively withdrew his blade—he didn't intend to take Georgia's life."],["","However, in the next second, Georgia's ST tilted entirely to the left, and the blade that Crocodile hadn't fully withdrawn directly sliced open the outer shell of Georgia's cockpit. As the blazing top light illuminated Georgia's face, Crocodile was momentarily dazed—"],["","Had they... met somewhere before?"],["","Before he could even react, the cockpit flooded with red warning alerts. A violent jolt slammed through the pilot cabin—Georgia had already locked onto the right arm joint of his ST."],["","Throughout the entire match, Georgia rarely initiated an attack, spending most of the time scurrying around like a lizard. But now the lizard has transformed into a dragon, and the Crocodile almost instantly heard the crisp sound of its joints undergoing transformation."],["Crocodile","N-no!"],["","He staggered back in a panic, but Georgia was faster. She twisted his arm guard the wrong way and snapped it clean off. The blade slipped from his grip and fell midair—exactly as she'd anticipated. She caught it, spun it in one fluid motion, and drove it straight toward Crocodile's cockpit."],["","Slash—! Blinding, high-temperature sparks erupted inside the cockpit. Crocodile roared and slammed the stick all the way back, his ST rocketing in reverse—barely avoiding having the cockpit skewered clean through."],["","There's still a chance—still a chance! Crocodile rapidly punched parameters into the control core. His cockpit was damaged, sure—but that girl's cockpit was completely exposed. One more strike. Just one more, and it would be over—"],["","A strong tremor suddenly surrounded Crocodile from all directions. He instinctively turned his attention to the display screen, which had cracked like a spider web. However, before he could see what was happening, a huge blade tip was already thrust in front of him."],["","On the screen, Georgia's ST is falling towards him entirely, and he belatedly feels a strong sense of weightlessness, as if his terrified soul is being squeezed to the surface of his body."],["Crocodile","... Madman. You're a madman—!"],["","She was using the sheer weight of her own ST to slam him down! But her cockpit had no outer armor left—falling from this height would kill her first. Just to win… was she really willing to go that far?!"],["Georgia","Easy… easy now…"],["","The massive sound of tearing steel exploded next to Crocodile's ears, and the intense light from the incandescent lamp pierced into his eyes through the widening gap in front of him. That person... that madman is still tearing open the shell of his cockpit!"],["","His ST's shell was specially made with high-strength alloy, but that lunatic tore it open like a bag of chips - Crocodile saw her ST's arms turning red, almost ready to explode. It turned out she had been waiting for this moment all along."],["","She overclocked all the power she had gathered into the energy conduits of her arms, allowing her to enhance the arm armor's performance in a very short time, destroy his arm joints, and tear open his pilot cabin. But she also turned herself into a ticking time bomb!"],["","The scene in front of the Crocodile became increasingly blurred, and his intuition told him he was about to hit bottom. His fingers instinctively pressed a button."],["","The moment the airbag deployed, Georgia's ST thrust its sword into the ground, halting the tipping motion, but she was thrown out of the cockpit due to the immense inertia—"],["","Boom——!!"],["","His ST collapsed completely, and the violent shaking made Crocodile feel as if his entire body was being hammered, even with the buffering of the airbags. Yet, he felt relieved because he was still the winner of this duel..."],["","Now he just needs to compose himself to receive the applause and cheers from the audience—"],["Audience Member A","Wildfire! Wildfire—!!!"],["Audience Member B","It's her! Well done! Wildfire!!"],["Audience Member A","Drag him out and take him down! Wildfire! Wildfire!"],["","Wha... What? Is he deaf from a concussion? Why aren't they shouting his name...? Wildfire? Who the hell is Wildfire?!"],["","With a bang, an airbag erupted. Another bang, and light appeared in Crocodile's vision again. He saw everything clearly—the crazy woman with flamboyant red hair was aiming the barrel of her gun at his head."],["","…Who—? A m-madwoman! That crazy woman isn't dead… she didn't die from the fall—! S-she planned it from the start… she was using his safety airbag!"],["","Rage surged through Crocodile as he shouted in fury—but in that instant, a rush of heat flooded his mind, dragging up a long-forgotten memory… Damn it. What the hell was that?!"],["Georgia","ESD-314, it has very low energy consumption, but it is also very fragile. You should prepare an additional alloy protective shell for it—if you can't prevent others from grabbing it... heh."],["","She coughed twice, then jumped off the ST, swaying in place to alleviate the intense discomfort from the concussion."],["","A tidal wave of boos rose from the crowd. They were all condemning her for not killing Crocodile. This incredible showdown was missing just one thing—a blood-soaked, perfect finish."],["","But she clearly had no interest in satisfying the crowd."],["Crocodile","G-Georgia! It's you—!"],["","A shocked roar came from behind. Georgia paused for a moment, but she neither turned back nor spoke. She simply stopped briefly and then left."],["","Crocodile lay completely limp in the battered cockpit, and after a long while, let out a sigh of relief as if surviving a disaster."],["","That Georgia... That ruthless, cold, merciless Georgia didn't choose to kill him after all... He was unbelievably lucky today."],["","Wait."],["","Was it because... he sheathed his sword at that moment? Because he didn't release his killing intent, Georgia ultimately chose to hold back...?"],["Crocodile","Tch... Heh... Hahaha... Who would've thought someone like you would actually talk about fairness..."],["","Bang—a stack of photos was slammed in front of the repair shop staff."],["","The person spread the photos out like a deck of cards. The employee glanced over them. The photos were close-ups of ST parts, which seemed to be a record of a set of arm guards when combined."],["Repair Shop Staff","Is there any part that needs repair, customer?"],["Gutzman","You should be curious about this stack of photos unless you've seen them before me."],["Repair Shop Staff","......"],["","Recalling something unknown, a hint of fear appeared on his face."],["Gutzman","I know you have the means to identify the special markings on these modified goods. I need to know whose hand these markings on the arm guards came from."],["Repair Shop Staff","And then find the buyer of these arm guards?"],["Gutzman","You know? Seems like you're quite smart."],["Repair Shop Staff","It's not that I'm smart."],["","The employee raised their left hand and right foot, both in casts."],["Repair Shop Staff","Sigh... Several groups have come to interrogate me harshly these past few days... But I was telling the truth before that—I really don't know."],["","Gutzman quietly watched him, making his hair stand on end."],["Repair Shop Staff","...I'm not lying to you, customer. We often receive parts for repair, so we are indeed familiar with many modification shops' marks in the market, but I really don't know about this arm guard."],["Repair Shop Staff","Never handled it, never even seen it. Maybe it's made by those guys who only supply to high-end clientele...? You should find someone more knowledgeable or with broader connections to help you..."],["","The voice of the repair shop staff grows quieter, as boundless fear gradually arises in his heart. Is he going to lose a hand or foot again today?"],["Gutzman","I'll leave a contact number. If you hear anything, let me know."],["Repair Shop Staff","Sigh—"],["","The repair shop staff tried to stop him, but couldn't prevent him from swiftly snatching pen and paper from the counter."],["","Gutzman silently begins to write. Outside, the noise gradually rises, like a tide surging towards the street outside this small shop. But inside the shop, it's eerily quiet, making people uneasy."],["Repair Shop Staff","Uh—uh, i-it's… it's over over there."],["","Gutzman doesn't respond, and a string of numbers slowly appears on the paper."],["Repair Shop Staff","You know, sir, right across the street is one of the most famous ST arenas around here—\"Underground Steam.\" Ever heard of it? They run ST duels every day. Pick the right fighter, place the right bet, and you could get rich overnight."],["Repair Shop Staff","Today's duel has been promoted for a long time, featuring the undefeated champion Crocodile from \"Underground Steam\" against the newcomer dark horse Wildfire!"],["Repair Shop Staff","I saw the poster, and that Wildfire is actually a red-haired woman! It's truly incredible. Although defeating Crocodile can earn a very substantial prize, it's amazing that a woman has the courage to challenge the strongest guy..."],["Repair Shop Staff","I don't know who won this duel, but I think it was probably Crocodile, after all, he's my idol..."],["Gutzman","Contact information."],["","Gutzman didn't react to the repair shop staff's rambling, he just pushed the written note in front of him and slammed a cloth bag onto the counter."],["Gutzman","This is the deposit for the information."],["Gutzman","Remember to contact me then—don't play tricks, I've memorized your face, and there are a thousand ways to deal with your betrayal."],["Repair Shop Staff","Uh...Alright."],["","Gutzman stepped out of the repair shop, leaning against the brick wall by the door to light a cigarette. As the crowd passed by, there was a hint of wistfulness in his eyes."],["","The trail ends here. Where should he go next?"],["","Apparently, Harpy had anticipated this situation, which is why they decided to spend a fortune using mercenaries to capture that bandit."],["","Mercenaries have their own channels for obtaining information, making them more efficient at finding or capturing people. But unfortunately..."],["","Unfortunately, Gutzman hasn't been working solo for long, and his foundation is far less solid than those of the well-established mercenary groups. He can only obtain information in such a simple way... It turns out this approach is indeed inefficient, as someone has already gotten ahead of him."],["","Calm down… calm down… Gutzman. It's not the end yet…"],["","He took a deep drag of his cigarette, exhaling a cloud of smoke—a hooded figure quickly passed in front of him, dispersing the smoke."],["","His nose twitched as he caught the scent of blood mingling with the smoke. The distant silhouette resembled an old acquaintance, and Gutzman was hesitant to be certain, but upon seeing the red hair blown away by the wind... he quickly snuffed out his cigarette and chased after."],["Gutzman","Georgia! Wait! Georgia! It's me!"],["","The person didn't pause for a moment, forcing Gutzman to quicken his pace and block her path."],["Gutzman","It's me, Georgia, please wait."],["Georgia","Step aside, Gutzman."],["Gutzman","What are you doing here? You... you're the \"Wildfire\" who challenged the \"Crocodile\"?!"],["Georgia","That's none of your business."],["Gutzman","Is it true that something happened to Iguana? I heard you've been having trouble with enemies lately..."],["Georgia","That's none of your concern, Gutzman. You're no longer a member of the Iguana."],["Gutzman","No, Georgia, if that's the case... listen to me first, Harpy recently issued a ten-million-level bounty, as long as we catch that thief—"],["","Gutzman pulls out a close-up photo and holds it in front of Georgia."],["Gutzman","This is the ST part he left at the scene at the time. If we follow this clue, we can definitely find him, and then…"],["Georgia","I'm not interested, Gutzman. No matter how much time you spend explaining, it's a waste of breath. Step aside."],["","Georgia sidesteps and walks forward, quickly leaving Gutzman behind."],["Gutzman","Georgia—! This bounty is not a small amount. Even if you don't do it for yourself, think about the Iguana brothers. Wouldn't they appreciate an extra income?"],["","Georgia finally stopped, and Gutzman breathed a sigh of relief as he caught up again. Before he could get close, Georgia spoke."],["Georgia","I'm not surprised at all that you would come to me again, Gutzman, because your desires and ambitions are beyond ordinary."],["Georgia","I don't blame you for the betrayal of Iguana for greater benefits, but I will never let the Iguana become your tool for profit. Do you understand?"],["Gutzman","...Georgia."],["","Georgia didn't look back, nor did she intend to pay any more attention to Gutzman, leaving the place like the wind."],["","Gutzman watched her receding figure blur into the distance and suddenly clenched his teeth."],["Gutzman","Such a good opportunity... Georgia, but you're still as rigid as ever."],["Gutzman","But it doesn't matter. You'll agree in the end."],["Gutzman Mercenary","We've finally tracked down Iguana's hideout. Split up and move—don't let Giorgia spot us."],["Recruit","Wait, wait! Bro, I still can't believe it. The boss really wants us to take on Georgia?"],["Recruit","That's the famous Iguana Mercenary Group! When I was getting started, Georgia was already at the top of her game! Challenging her now is a death wish!"],["Gutzman Mercenary","What are you afraid of? Times have changed, and the boss has his reasons. We just need to follow orders."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Besides, we have equipment provided by Harpy for this operation—did you bring it?"],["Recruit","Got it all packed. It's said to be a \"Nano Corrector\" that can help with the ST's performance stability... Is it really that effective?"],["Gutzman Mercenary","As long as we have it, we just need to wait for the boss's signal."],["Recruit","But Georgia, she..."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Shut up, newbie."],["Recruit","...Hey, buddy..."],["","The communication channel falls silent for a few seconds, followed by a long sigh."],["Gutzman Mercenary","I know you're a bit worried—not just you, many people are concerned about the success of this raid, after all, we're facing a very formidable opponent."],["Gutzman Mercenary","I don't want to say anything like \"for the mercenary group\" or \"for honor\"... Let's just say it's for everyone's own sake."],["Gutzman Mercenary","No one becomes a mercenary just to die. We just want to survive. But on Milkhama, if you want to live properly, you're forced to do things you fear—things you'd rather never face."],["Gutzman Mercenary","There will be a battle between us and Malcolm eventually. Do you want to end up as minced meat under Malcolm's war machines?"],["Recruit","...No."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Then let's follow the boss's plan... and fight to win this round."],["","The communication channel was silent for a moment, then a few voices gradually echoed, growing louder. Everyone was somewhat inspired, and the legendary Georgia seemed unable to stop them anymore."],["","In contrast to the atmosphere here, tensions were already rising not far from them."],["Georgia","Stop, Gutzman, are you testing my limits?"],["","Gutzman loosened and tightened his grip on the lever repeatedly. The radar showed at least ten thermal reactions across the bridge, indicating that this was indeed the new base of the Iguana Mercenary Group."],["","Georgia might tolerate his following along the way, but there's absolutely no way she would allow a 'traitor' to set foot on Iguana's territory again."],["Gutzman","Georgia... I don't want to test you, nor do I wish to pressure you. I just feel that we still have room for negotiation."],["Gutzman","Our cooperation will be based on fairness and justice. I absolutely have no intention of using you to achieve my goals."],["Gutzman","As a former member of the Iguanas, believe it or not, I never intended to drag it into the abyss."],["Georgia","Enough. I don't have time to listen to your long-winded speech. Right now, I just need you to get out of my sight."],["","Georgia is somewhat impatient, the injuries she sustained in the arena are still affecting her thoughts, and she must rest immediately."],["Gutzman","......"],["","Gutzman's ST slowly backed away—then came to an abrupt stop."],["Gutzman","I thought you, of all people, would understand me, Georgia. None of us has it easy—we risk our lives just to live a little easier. So why are you still so hung up on me leaving the Iguana?"],["Georgia","I told you to get lost—"],["","Georgia's head hurt even more, and she had no time to explain further. Gutzman might be able to win her over in the future, but right now she just wanted to shoot and drive him away. However, every bullet of the Iguana Mercenary Group was precious now. Was Gutzman worth it?"],["Gutzman","I didn't betray you, nor did I betray the Iguana. I just found a place where I can become better! You always consider everyone, so why can't you understand my choice?"],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia frowned and leaned back, taking a deep breath."],["","After all that useless talk, he finally managed to say something useful."],["","\"Everyone\"... Yes. When Gutzman proposed cooperation to her, she was indeed tempted, not for anything else, but for the iguana that is no longer what it used to be... \"Everyone\" needs that money, it's just..."],["Gutzman","Sigh, I implore you to reconsider, Georgia. Although we have some differences in management philosophy, this won't affect our cooperation."],["","Georgia remained silent for a long time. She opened her mouth, just about to say something when she heard a loud eruption."],["Georgia","Enemy attack? All units, stay alert—"],["","As soon as the words left her mouth, Georgia felt a violent shake in the pilot cabin—the sensor screen showed her right arm had been blown off."],["Gutzman","Danger! Georgia!"],["","Gutzman piloted the ST swiftly to cover her, while opening the mechanical backpack mounted on its back torso, where a pair of brand-new, dazzling ST arm guards lay neatly."],["Gutzman","Just the things Harpy gave me can come in handy. Quickly call someone to help put them on! The enemy could attack from anywhere, so hurry up!"],["Georgia","…How is it such a coincidence? I just lost my arm and you have replacement parts?"],["Gutzman","In such a critical moment, do you really want to sort everything out with me before facing the enemy? Don't be foolish! I'll explain later, it truly is just a friendly sponsorship from Harpy—"],["Gutzman","Be careful during the connection. The energy output of the arm interface needs to be adjusted to overloaded first. Heh, this model has its own quirks."],["","In the distance, members of the Gutzman Mercenary group are rapidly approaching."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Attention, the boss has given special instructions. This ruse must be convincing, so don't hold back when facing the boss's mechs!"],["Recruit","Understood, leave it to us!"],["Gutzman Mercenary","Alright—! Big plans, big moves. Let's make something awesome happen! For ourselves—let's begin!"]],"468309401":[["Gutzman","Stop it all—!"],["","Gutzman raised his machine gun and sprayed at the mercenaries preparing to finish off Georgia, finally clearing a space."],["","At this moment, his condition wasn't good either, with his entire right arm sparking, but for some reason, he still insisted on standing in front of Georgia."],["Georgia","Who sent you..."],["","Georgia's voice was hoarse, contemplating how to severance."],["","This raid was too terrible, if she hadn't been injured, she wouldn't have ended up in such a situation!"],["Gutzman Mercenary","Georgia, you've made countless enemies. Do you really remember who they all are?"],["Gutzman Mercenary","This time, we've finally found a chance to corner you. You can't escape!"],["","With a series of clicks, the remaining STs with combat power raised their guns again."],["","In the pilot cabin, Georgia's face was pale, and her seat was covered in blood. With trembling fingertips, she pressed a button to switch to an encrypted channel."],["Georgia","Go, those of you who can still move, prepare to retreat—take Hannas with you, leave quickly, I can hold them off a little longer."],["Georgia Mercenary","No way, boss, I'm staying here to fight with you until the very end!"],["Georgia","This is not a joke! We might all die here, we can't all lose our lives here, understand?"],["Georgia","Take my medicine to Hannas, then you retreat to a safe place. You have to trust me—how could these scumbags possibly kill me?"],["Georgia Mercenary","Boss, we can't let you go alone—"],["","The sound of bullets suddenly erupted as Gutzman fired to take Control... Georgia pulled the lever, slowly maneuvering the ST to stand up."],["","Maybe it's time... Georgia closed her eyes."],["","Beep—beep—beep—multiple red dots suddenly appear on the radar detection screen, rapidly approaching here."],["Gutzman","Don't forget I'm still here. You're facing more than just the Iguana Mercenary Group—"],["Gutzman Mercenary","Dang it! You still have a backup plan?!"],["Georgia Mercenary","So many ST signals?! Are they... reinforcements?!"],["Gutzman","Want to continue? My people are on their way. If you have the confidence for another fight, I'm happy to oblige."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Damn it—! Retreat for now! There will be more opportunities later!"],["","The team that was just boasting and arrogant quickly organized and withdrew from the scene. Their departure was so swift that it seemed like sparks were about to fly from the ground, as if they were afraid to confront those inexhaustible troops."],["","Seeing the enemy retreat, everyone opened the pilot cabin doors. Thick white steam first rushed out from the gaps in the cabin and quickly dissipated into the air."],["Georgia Mercenary","Boss! Are you okay? Lean on me a bit."],["","Georgia rejected the support of her subordinates, standing tall with her spear, watching Gutzman slowly approach her."],["Georgia","You have so many people, yet you still want to cooperate with me?"],["Gutzman","...Fake, that was a false signal I forged, I don't have that many people under me."],["Gutzman","Your information is always very well-informed, you should know that after I got out, things haven't been going well for me."],["Georgia","Heh, it's already enough, haven't you connected with the military? You have some sort of protection."],["Gutzman","...Just some dirty work, they only see me as a useful gun, a obedient hound."],["Gutzman","I don't want to be obedient anymore, so they went to find the next dog."],["Georgia","......"],["Gutzman","Georgia..."],["","The red-haired woman across from him gazed at him calmly."],["","Gutzman knew that even though Georgia now needed to lean on a spear to stand steadily, if he did anything to anger or provoke her, she could still spring to life and take his life in an instant."],["Gutzman","I know everything that's happened so far has filled you with doubt..."],["Gutzman","I don't want to hide it from you. I was working so hard to help just now because I hope you'll seriously consider working with me—putting aside any biases, you know very well what the choice for maximum benefit is right now."],["Gutzman","I need your connections, so I'm asking for your help. Once it's done, you can decide how to distribute the bounty. How about it?"],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia lightly kicked the gun barrel into her hand, and the iguana crowd surrounded her as they left, leaving only a light remark lingering in the air."],["Georgia","I'll give it some thought."],["","The night descends."],["","Georgia gently pushes the door open, and the hallway light casts a square halo inside. The person lying in bed turns their head, seemingly awakened by the sound."],["Georgia","Wake up, Hannas. Every time I come by, you're out cold—boring as hell."],["Hannas","Hey... Well, next time, come early..."],["","He wears a respirator, his voice somewhat enfeebled, like a flickering candle. Georgia closes the door, takes out several vials from her bag, and flicks them with her fingers. The pale yellow liquid inside clings to the walls briefly before settling back down."],["Georgia","NEX-5D... A doctor said this medicine might be of some help, let's give it a try."],["Hannas","Pretty expensive, huh?"],["Georgia","Not too bad."],["Hannas","You're lying... Hehehe... But fine, whatever you say."],["Hannas","As for me... I don't care anymore. When those two bullets went through my lungs... I really thought I was going to die there, but here I am, living a few more days... It's damn worth it."],["","Georgia didn't say a word. She picked up Hannas's arm, which was almost covered with needle marks, paused for a moment, and then slowly injected the medical reagents into the vein."],["Hannas","Today's opponent... aren't they annoying? Oh... look at you... that little face of yours is even paler than mine."],["Georgia","Not bad, a bit weaker than you."],["","Georgia slowly sat down on the ground, leaned her head back, and looked at the yellowing ceiling while resting on the bed."],["Hannas","Of course, who am I? The famous... Deputy of Georgia, the Iguana Mercenary Head!"],["Georgia","He recognized me, maybe we've crossed paths in the past."],["Hannas","Real... or fake...? How can you be sure they're from the underworld? What if... what if they're your colleagues from the Defense Force... heh heh..."],["","Georgia closed her eyes."],["Georgia","Sorry, Hannas, I've been disconnected from the Defense Force."],["Georgia","After the Vesper incident, the entire East Island is in chaos. I don't know what happened over there, otherwise I should have been able to apply to transfer you to the military hospital for the best treatment. It's my..."],["Hannas","Boring... Georgia... It's really boring when you say things like that."],["Hannas","Everyone has their fate... Georgia... Maybe I should have died in that fire twenty years ago... Heh heh heh, you saved me once when you were just a little girl... Now I have nothing to complain about."],["","Hannas reached out his hand and gently patted Georgia on the top of her head."],["Hannas","Enough, Georgia, I know what I'm doing."],["Hannas","Don't go to the arena anymore. The earnings aren't even as much as a fraction of what we used to make in a single job. I can't believe you're actually willing to play with those amateurs."],["Hannas","Do something worthwhile and follow the path an iguana should take."],["Hannas","...Huh? Georgia, the medicine you brought back is truly amazing. Did you notice that I'm speaking more smoothly now?"],["","Georgia tilted her head to avoid Hannas' hand and silently took out her sidearm to start cleaning it."],["Georgia","...Don't tell me it's just a last burst of energy, you fool."],["Hannas","Ha... You really know how to make things unpleasant. By the way, I heard Gutzman wants to collaborate with us?"],["Georgia","Hmm, I'm considering it."],["Hannas","Sigh, things got pretty ugly when you guys fell out..."],["Georgia","I remember it clearly. That's why I'm still weighing it."],["Hannas","Be careful… I'm worried he'll set you up."],["Georgia","He's very persistent... Maybe he truly has no other choice but to seek cooperation with someone he once despised."],["Hannas","But you're not like that, you have other paths to take, Georgia..."],["","Georgia's hand suddenly stops cleaning the gun. She looks at the dark muzzle, and countless black holes aiming at her flash through her mind from earlier in the day."],["Georgia","We almost faced total annihilation today, Hannas."],["Georgia","I know there are countless intriguing coincidences, but these coincidences also show me that the iguana is teetering."],["Georgia","I don't have time. I can't just sit here and wait for news from the Defense Force."],["Hannas","..."],["","The two remained silent for a long time. Georgia heard Hannas's breathing become heavy."],["Hannas","Sigh..."],["Hannas","Let's go... Georgia, leave Milkhama... take those you care about and leave this dull place..."],["Georgia","Ha, have you already fallen asleep? Why are you starting to talk in your sleep?"],["Hannas","Tsk... Look at you now... Look at how down and out you've become... If you leave Milkhama, with your skills, you could thrive in anything you do..."],["Georgia","...Do you know what I want to do?"],["Hannas","Yeah... You want to be a forest ranger... You told me when you were drunk... pulling on my ear..."],["Georgia","...I said those things too."],["Hannas","Ha... Haha... Hahaha... But, but... I think maybe... you're bluffing..."],["Georgia","...I'm not bluffing."],["Hannas","Hehe... Being... being a ranger means... living alone... with a gun... in the mountains..."],["Georgia","Take a break, Hannas, haven't you noticed the effects are wearing off?"],["Hannas","Geo, Georgia... you... you won't go, because you—"],["","Because you're afraid of *****."],["Georgia","Really? When did you hear me say that?"],["Hannas","......"],["Georgia","Hannas?"],["Hannas","......"],["Georgia","......"],["Georgia","Has the medicine worn off?"],["Hannas","......"],["Georgia","Hmm, then sleep well."],["","Georgia leaned against the bedside, slowly closing her eyes. Her face twitched faintly, an uncontrollable tremor emanating from deep within her body, and a line of scalding tears rolled from her tightly shut eyes."],["","...Good night."],["","Georgia pursed her lips and somewhat awkwardly handed over the iodine and bandages."],["Georgia","...Sorry, Officer."],["Officer","Sorry for what? Sorry for not letting me strangle you just now?"],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia couldn't help but touch her neck. She hadn't had the chance to observe it closely, but she was sure there must be a circle of purplish bruises."],["","She hadn't forgotten the pain of suffocating and near death just now, and her gaze at the officer was mixed with subtle fear."],["Officer","You did well, using your flexibility to wrap around my neck and force me to let go. In that situation, you had no choice, so don't feel guilty."],["Officer","Haven't recovered yet? Take a good rest first."],["","The officer slowly stood up, staggering a few steps before steadying himself. Clearly, Georgia's retaliation was quite powerful."],["Officer","But what I just said wasn't part of the test. You might want to think it over, Georgia. Otherwise, you'll eventually face everything you just went through, and there won't be another chance to get back up."],["Georgia","I've faced it countless times before... officer."],["Officer","But now you have another choice, don't you?"],["","The officer patted her shoulder and walked towards the training room door."],["Georgia","Is it because my abilities haven't been recognized by you?"],["","The officer turned back."],["Officer","No, compared to your first training, you've transformed completely. You're diligent, and I can feel your determination to complete the mission."],["Officer","If you keep practicing, you'll become the best subordinate I've ever had."],["Georgia","Then why did you suddenly want to back out? You once said I was perfect for this mission—I grew up in the mercenary group and know everything about them."],["Georgia","I can be the eyes of the defense force, or I can be the blade of the defense force..."],["","Georgia's voice grew louder, and she felt a sharp pain in her head—a side effect of oxygen deprivation. She knew this would happen, but she was eager to express her stance."],["","The officer sighed and walked back to invite her to sit down together."],["Officer","After you agreed to take on this mission... I dreamed of Nora many times."],["","Georgia froze. Nora… her former teammate. They trained together, deployed together, were once surrounded by bandits together… and in the end, only she survived."],["Officer","My sister has cursed me in my dreams more than once, asking why I sent you on such a dangerous mission."],["Georgia","That's a mix of your imagination and memory, affecting your brain to some extent. Nora is dead, she won't truly enter your dreams."],["Officer","......"],["Georgia","...Sorry, I'm used to speaking this way... I just hope you don't dwell too much on your dreams, I'm fine."],["Officer","I do."],["Georgia","?"],["Officer","We've sparred 77 times, Georgia. In 53 of those, if I had gone a bit further, you would have died."],["Georgia","Sorry, I promise I'll become stronger after this—"],["Officer","That's not what I want to tell you."],["","The officer's gaze suddenly turned sharp, and Georgia felt as if she was being aimed at by the grim reaper, her hair standing on end—Gerard is the most outstanding sniper, and the prey he targets rarely escapes."],["Officer","If you truly become a mercenary again, becoming the shadow of the defense force in the dark, as long as one of those 53 attacks succeeds, you won't be able to return."],["Georgia","......"],["Georgia","I-I can handle it."],["","She spoke, her voice dry and hoarse. Maybe she didn't truly have that kind of confidence deep down—but she knew she couldn't afford to falter now."],["Officer","\"Death\" cannot be resolved. Once it occurs, it is an irrevocable loss. Nora was once as outstanding as you, but now she has become a formless heap of ashes."],["Georgia","...Sorry, officer, Nora was trying to save me at the time..."],["Officer","You don't need to... feel sorry, Georgia. If I were there at the time, I would have made the same choice as Nora. Protecting our companions is our duty and obligation."],["Officer","Nora hopes you survive, and you don't want to die easily either, Georgia. So stay away from those dangers that will devour you."],["","His hand suddenly trembled secretly, as if recalling the endless weak pulse of Georgia after being pushed to the limit these days. With a little more force, Georgia would become a soul under his hand."],["","If time keeps passing like this... maybe that day will eventually come? But when he thinks of that day, he feels genuinely sad."],["","When selecting the person for the task, he carefully read through the resumes of each candidate, and Georgia was the only girl among them. At that time, she was very petite, with her red hair standing out prominently among the pile of photos."],["","The reason Georgia was chosen is probably her background—she hails from \"Frida Town,\" a mercenary town that has already been exterminated by the Defense Forces. Many people think that someone who grew up accustomed to the mercenary life would fit right back into the mercenary group like a fish in water."],["","But he disagrees. The downfall of Frida was due to Georgia's collusion with the Defense Forces, and the fiery girl personally burned that sinful land to the ground... And now they want her to return to such a world?"],["","And then one day, she was brutally murdered by some ruthless people, ending her short and frantic life. No one cared that she didn't actually want to die, and no one knew that she worked so hard in the Defense Forces just to earn herself a protection."],["","In the end, the Defense Forces she trusted did not protect her, but instead let her rest eternally in the land she despised... It shouldn't have been this way. If they still had the ability, they shouldn't have let this happen."],["","Otherwise... how sad this would be."],["Officer","Let's put this on hold for now. I'll discuss the next steps of the mission with my superiors. You get some rest."],["","The officer stood up, supporting himself on his knees, while Georgia, pale-faced, quickly leaned forward to grab his hem."],["Georgia","...Death isn't that frightening, sir, not to me."],["Officer","......"],["Georgia","\"Frida Town\" is notorious, yet it's my hometown. My memories begin with death, sir. Taking lives and preventing one's life from being taken is as natural as breathing. So I'm not afraid of death."],["Georgia","When you gave me this task, you once told me that every step I take in the darkness rebuilds new hope. I've always remembered those words, and they make me feel that everything I'm doing now is worthwhile."],["Georgia","I'm not afraid to die, sir."],["","The man's gaze flickered. He reached out and grasped Georgia's wrist, the steady and powerful pulse transmitted through the thin skin to his palm, like a war drum."],["Georgia","I just don't want to be powerless—unable to change anything—only to be swept away by the tide of war. Living in a haze, born in confusion, and dying for nothing."],["Officer","You..."],["Georgia","If I can still do something... I... I don't want to die \"alone\"... sir."],["","Beep—beep beep—beep—beep beep—"],["","Georgia opened her eyes, feeling a bit dazed."],["Georgia Mercenary","Hey? Boss? Are you awake? It's time for your meeting with Gutzman, he's waiting for you in the hangar."],["Georgia Mercenary","We've prepared everything else you need, so if you're awake, just head over."],["","*beep*"],["Georgia","......"],["Georgia","So it was just a dream..."],["","Tell me, who else has ordered parts of this type from you!"],["","I... I've already told you, I know I've told you... It's really only the people on the list, there's no one else..."],["","List? You still have the nerve to mention a list? Look at the names you've written, they're clearly just codenames!"],["","Innocent, I'm innocent, boss! In our line of work, the last thing our clients want is for their true identities to be known. We've been using code names for years!"],["","So, who has been ordering these parts from you recently?"],["","Hey, hey—! I know! I know! Someone asked me the same question—"],["","After I pointed out the code name, he quickly guessed the person's identity. It was... it was \"Douglas\"! \"Douglas\"—!!!"],["","Georgia pressed the pause button, and the record ended there."],["","Gutzman glanced at Georgia, only to find her staring back at him. The two shared a silent moment across the space, clearly both harboring some unknown thoughts."],["Gutzman","Nice move, Georgia. I didn't expect you to find them so quickly."],["Georgia","Just the owner of a parts shop, with no one to protect him. By the time my people found him, he was already covered in bruises... Fortunately, he could still speak."],["Georgia","The bandit behind the crime turned out to be Douglas... Do you have any leads?"],["Gutzman","It's not important. What's important now is that someone beat us to it. Luckily, Douglas is usually cunning and cautious, with many hideouts. He shouldn't be easy to find."],["Gutzman","It's time to consider what to do next."],["Georgia","...I can take you to him."],["Gutzman","Really? How are you going to find him?"],["Georgia","Gutzman, I chose a hideout for the iguana that eliminated all possible factors of discovery, but unfortunately, an unknown enemy still found us... It seems there's no such thing as a secret that can't be uncovered in this world."],["","Gutzman's heart skipped a beat. Georgia... did she find out something?"],["Gutzman","......"],["Gutzman","You're right, then I'll be waiting for your news."],["","Gutzman stood up to leave, but halfway through, he had a sudden inspiration and stopped in his tracks."],["Gutzman","Did you take care of that shop owner?"],["Georgia","...I've already handled it, you don't need to worry."],["Georgia","Three days from now, I'll inform you where to meet."]],"468313101":[["Rena","Increase pulse injection by 20%... temperature control remains unchanged... stabilize matrix generation, activate perception receiver."],["","Rena flipped a switch, and the screen beside her began scrolling with recorded experiment data."],["","Rena quietly watched for two minutes, extracting several key data points to compare with previous sets, finding almost no discrepancies."],["","She smiled at the protective glass in front of her, then suddenly thought of something else, and the curve of her mouth fell."],["Jon","You've been sneaking around here for days. Have you come up with any results?"],["Rena","J-Jon—?!"],["","Jon emerged from the darkness, holding two cups of coffee, and handed one to Rena."],["Jon","Don't be so surprised, I'm the only one who noticed you here."],["Rena","You scared me... I thought I'd been completely exposed."],["Jon","You're so cautious, always coming over when Douglas isn't paying attention. How could you be exposed?"],["Jon","He's been away from the base for two days. This place is hot and stuffy, only you can stand it... Why the long face? Is your research not going well?"],["Rena","I extracted some alloy from those arm guards. They... I can't describe it well, come over and take a look."],["","Rena stepped aside to let Jon into the observation area in front of the protection glass, as the experiment was entering a critical phase."],["","A small piece of dark alloy is placed at the center of the lab table. Gradually, it starts to spin with the table, faster and faster, until suddenly, in a millisecond, the entire alloy shatters with a bang without any Omen."],["Jon","What!? This..."],["Rena","Don't rush, keep watching."],["","The lab table stops spinning, covered with sesame-like debris. Under Jon's Gaze, the dark specks quickly start wriggling like leeches, converging towards the center."],["","Their speed is fast, and in no time, they gather and form an alloy very similar to the previous one."],["Jon","What is this... substance... thing... stuff...??"],["Rena","......"],["Rena","Earlier, I applied high-intensity microwave energy to it, simulating the damage it would experience on the battlefield. Due to heat accumulation and localized overheating, as you can see, it first cracked and then completely shattered."],["Jon","B-But it..."],["Rena","Yes, under the influence of some external force, it restored itself, but there is a certain degree of alteration compared to its original form."],["Jon","It crawls like a bug! It..."],["Rena","Theoretically, metal is non-living, so it shouldn't be a bug—I suppose it must be some kind of... core? Inner force? Or perhaps something more mysterious that is pulling it to complete the operation restoration."],["Jon","I think the concept of bugs crawling towards a bug mother is easier to understand... Well, I'm just imagining."],["Rena","...Sigh, I'm clueless too."],["Rena","This thing is beyond my knowledge... Where did Harpy get this batch from?"],["Jon","Could it be another new technology developed by Obsidian? They've been deeply involved in Arashi matter for years, maybe they've recently made some new discoveries but haven't made them public, just created some prototypes to test the market reaction? I think..."],["","Jon was talking endlessly about his speculations, but Rena's thoughts had already drifted to somewhere unknown, her expression becoming vacant."],["Jon","...so don't worry too much, we'll eventually find out what this thing is."],["Rena","...could it be that there's an issue with my testing environment? If I reconnect it to the mecha, maybe I can get some new data to assist my analysis."],["Jon","What? Are you planning to put it back on the ST again? Rena, I have to remind you, this is very uncontrollable."],["Rena","It's okay, I won't use my own special ST. If something unexpected happens, it can be destroyed."],["Jon","I mean, what if it happens to be discovered by Douglas..."],["Jon","Sigh, never mind, I'll cover for you then. Come on, I'll help you put it on."],["","Tundra."],["","The iguana and the Gutzman Mercenary are rapidly advancing in the same direction."],["","Gutzman adjusted several driving parameters and then opened the locator to check how far they were from the destination."],["Georgia","Douglas might notice in advance, so we'd better split up. You take some people and block his retreat route."],["Gutzman","Understood... But speaking of which, we don't even know if he's been caught yet."],["Georgia","Not yet. This time he's gotten smarter and is hiding in an unexpected new place."],["Gutzman","And yet you found him, Georgia. I knew that as long as you were willing to help, all problems would be solved—"],["Georgia","It just so happens that someone knows his whereabouts, and I happen to have some connections with that person."],["Gutzman","Is...?"],["Georgia","Sand Whale, a recently rising information dealer."],["Georgia","Speaking of which, I thought Douglas would contact you, after all, you had worked together before... What happened, was it unpleasant at the time?"],["Gutzman","......"],["","Gutzman's expression changed slightly, somewhat surprised that Georgia knew he had crossed paths with Douglas. This was not good news."],["Gutzman","It's all... a long time ago. We haven't had much contact for a while."],["Gutzman","Besides, now he's the million-dollar target we're after, any connection between us doesn't matter anymore."],["Georgia","Heh, sounds like something you'd say."],["Georgia","Once we get the bounty, Douglas's team will be leaderless. What are your thoughts?"],["Gutzman","Whatever works, I'll follow your lead."],["Georgia","Hmm. We're almost there, get ready for battle."],["Rena","Data match rate 43%... As expected, they undergo changes that are imperceptible to the naked eye when in an independent state versus a docked state."],["Rena","Will it be different in combat mode?"],["Jon","...You're not thinking of a simulated battle, are you? That would be quite a commotion, we'd need a pretext first."],["Rena","What did Douglas go off to do, anyway?"],["Jon","He didn't say much, just said he was going to meet someone and find a way to get out of this situation."],["Rena","It took two days to meet someone? So slow..."],["Jon","If we keep the battle under half an hour and don't use heavy firepower, we shouldn't alert them."],["Rena","Then do it quick..."],["Predator Mercenary","Where are you? The patrol found someone coming, we're going to meet them. You keep an eye on those supplies."],["Rena","We've been discovered here?!"],["Jon","Got it, stay safe."],["Predator Mercenary","W-Wait! That's—That's the Iguana team! No, you need to come out and help, or we might not be able to handle Georgia."],["Rena","Georgia?!"],["","Rena and Jon exchanged a glance, seeing disbelief in each other's eyes."],["Rena","W-Well, we..."],["Predator Mercenary","Move it! Or we're all done for!"],["","After hesitating for a while, Rena finally nodded vigorously and quickly jumped onto the mech."],["Rena","Let's go, with this new equipment helping us, we might not lose to her!"],["Rena","Perfect, let's have a real battle and see what new discoveries we can make!"],["","The mercenaries outside the stronghold were all on high alert. It wasn't long before Rena saw a familiar ST on the monitor feed."],["Rena","As expected, it's Georgia..."],["","The mighty ST squad is stationed not far from the stronghold."],["Georgia","Rena? It's been a while! I can't believe you've joined Douglas's team."],["Rena","...If possible, I'd rather not fight you, Georgia."],["Georgia","I know, at least for now, you have no choice."],["Georgia","Come on, let's get straight to the point and find a chance to catch up later."]],"468313301":[["Gutzman","Is everything here?"],["Rena","...Everything's here, not a single item has been handed over."],["","After answering, Rena couldn't help but glance at Georgia standing at the front."],["","Since they were brought in, Georgia has remained silent, observing the entire base. From the placement of supplies to the location of emergency exits, from the damage to their mechs to Rena's hastily arranged makeshift lab."],["","She observed very carefully, and Rena even felt that the living waste they had produced over the past few days would be thoroughly analyzed by Georgia."],["Gutzman","Where's Douglas?"],["Rena","He left, it's been two days and he hasn't returned—we don't know where he went."],["Gutzman","Don't know? Or don't want to say?"],["Rena","I'm not lying to you—"],["Jon","We really don't know, but he's definitely coming back because he left these things here."],["Georgia","Harpy Commerce has been looking for you."],["","Georgia turned around and spoke unexpectedly."],["Jon","This news isn't unexpected, if I were them, I'd do the same."],["Georgia","You still accept reality so quickly, Jon."],["Jon","The premise of resistance is having the conditions to resist. Georgia, I know you won't let us leave easily."],["Georgia","Who said that?"],["Jon","......"],["Rena","...?"],["Gutzman","Georgia?"],["Georgia","Let's make a trade. I'll let you go, and you—"],["Jon","Help you catch Douglas?"],["Georgia","Smart."],["Jon","No, you're the one with the clever plan. Douglas isn't here, so it's just me and Rena with the most say."],["Jon","As long as we surrender, the others won't dare to resist you."],["Georgia","Heh... Jon, you should know that Douglas has nowhere to run. There are only two paths before you: either be detained and wait until Douglas is caught, then be handed over to Harpy for the bounty..."],["Georgia","After that, whether you live or die, or end up crippled or ruined, is unpredictable."],["Georgia","Or—work with me, and after we catch Douglas, I'll let you go."],["Rena","...You have strength in numbers, and if you decide to go back on your word after the deed is done, we would be powerless."],["Georgia","Indeed."],["Gutzman","......"],["","For a moment, everyone fell silent. In Georgia's art of language... Georgia has no art of language. Whether as an opponent or a teammate, negotiating under her lead makes people want to sigh."],["Georgia","I am the absolute victor of this battle, and I need not make any concessions to you through words or actions."],["Georgia","The proposal of this trade essentially offers you a faster path to freedom, and trades always come with risks."],["Georgia","How about it? Want to bet? Bet that Douglas will defeat us all upon his return, bet that the horned eagle will suddenly change its nature and forgive you for what you've done. Or perhaps..."],["Georgia","Bet that your former leader will let you go after a friendly cooperation."],["","Rena bit her lower lip, her gaze quickly sweeping over everyone's faces, her keen observation not missing the fleeting Interferents smile in Georgia's eyes."],["","Georgia was very confident and knew them well. When she proposed this Trade, she was already aware of their final Choice."],["Rena","May I propose an additional condition... no, a request?"],["Jon","Rena!"],["Rena","You are indeed the absolute victor of this battle, but your ultimate goal should be more than just winning this fight, right?"],["Georgia","......"],["Rena","I also believe that with your strength, Douglas is no match for you, but we both know how cunning Douglas can be..."],["Rena","If you don't take this opportunity to capture him in one fell swoop, but instead let him escape and become wary, it will actually waste a lot of your time entangling with him, won't it? Maybe... maybe it will even complicate matters, allowing others to get ahead."],["Georgia","What do you want?"],["Rena","I don't mean to threaten you, Georgia, I just have a request, and it's not difficult for you to accomplish—"],["Rena","I want a pair of arm guards from Harpy's supplies, just one pair will be enough."],["","Rena finished speaking and looked at Georgia with some nervousness. She had a deep respect for this woman, and this request was made under the strong drive of her scientific curiosity. In fact, it would be impossible for her to say it a second time under pressure."],["","Georgia... Would Georgia agree to her? Would she agree to what sounded quite like a threat?"],["","Georgia...?"],["","Douglas hid in a shadow, using binoculars to observe the situation at the stronghold."],["","He just got back and quickly noticed something was wrong. There were signs of a battle outside the base. Maybe someone had found this place. In this situation, he couldn't just rush in; if he ran into the enemy, there would be nowhere to run."],["","Now, he could only try to contact his subordinates to probe the situation before making any plans."],["","The camera didn't detect anything unusual, and finally, the call he had been making got a response—"],["Douglas","What the hell?! Where are you people?! What's the situation at the base?!"],["Rena","......"],["Rena","Boss, nothing's wrong."],["Douglas","Nothing's wrong with all those craters and shell casings outside? If you're going to fool me, at least pick a convincing reason!"],["Rena","Really, nothing's wrong. Those marks were made accidentally when I was experimenting with the batch from yesterday, using the horned eagle. Collected some combat data."],["Douglas","…You're not lying to me, are you?"],["Rena","Sigh. Are you nearby? Then take a good look, everyone is fine."],["","Douglas took a look, and sure enough, all the familiar faces had gathered by the window, looking around, perhaps searching for him."],["","But there was an indescribable feeling lingering in his heart. After years of living on the edge, his intuition told him that this place harbored a danger best avoided."],["Douglas","Tch, you wasteful woman, I'll deal with you later!"],["Douglas","Go and inform everyone to pack up and prepare to leave with me."],["Rena","Leave here? But where can we go now?"],["Douglas","I've made arrangements to leave Milkhama and lay low in Ovett. I refuse to believe that Harpy Commerce reach extends that far!"],["Rena","...Boss, why don't you come back for a bit? Packing up will take some time, and I'm worried you'll get impatient waiting outside."],["Douglas","Don't give me any excuses! There's not much stuff to pack, so hurry up and get it done! I'm waiting for you here."],["Rena","...Alright."],["","Douglas put away the communicator and used binoculars to check the situation at the base. Sure enough, after he gave the order, shadows occasionally flitted past the windows, likely moving things back and forth."],["","He breathed a slight sigh of relief and began the long wait."],["","After a while, the stronghold's gate opened, with a team of STs leading the way, surrounding several transport trucks loaded with their precious supplies."],["Douglas","Stop! Stop—!!"],["","Douglas ran out from the shadows, waving his hand as he headed towards the team."],["","His exclusive ride, Kong, was at the forefront of the team and quickly came to a halt upon hearing his call."],["Douglas","Who's in my ST? Get down here and make room—now!"],["","Sure enough, the Kong's pilot cabin hatch slowly opened. Douglas looked up, ready to wait for the pilot to operate Kong and bring him to the hatch. The pilot cabin was shrouded in shadow, and Douglas couldn't even call out a name to urge him to speed up."],["","Suddenly, a dark gun barrel extended from the hatch, leaving Douglas dumbfounded. His hands and feet reacted faster than his brain, and he turned to run!"],["","However, with a loud bang, Douglas's right leg was in severe pain, causing him to fall to the ground, his face acting as a brake."],["","He didn't look back, continuing to crawl forward using both hands and feet. A strong survival will drove him to find a safe zone. He quickly crawled into a shadow, looked up, and saw Georgia with her red hair flamboyant, looking down at him expressionlessly."],["Douglas","Georgia—?!!"],["","He could hardly believe it. He turned back toward the one who had hijacked his seat—Gutzman already had his gun raised, taking aim at him again."],["Douglas","You—?! You and Georgia actually—no! No! Gutzman! Don't shoot! Don't—ahhh!!!"],["","Blood quickly gushed from his left leg, merging with the blood from his right leg and seeping into the ground."],["Georgia","Enough, Gutzman, he can't run anymore."],["","Douglas gritted his teeth, trembling as he looked around at everyone present, the STs, and the transport vehicles, his eyes bursting with intense malice and hatred."],["Douglas","You heartless traitors! How dare you betray me?! You——!"],["","Douglas's voice was abruptly cut off—Georgia knocked him out with a kick."],["Georgia","Someone treat his wounds and give him a full dose of sedative. I don't need him conscious for what's next."],["","Gutzman jumps off Kong, followed by Rena and Jon, and the three of them come to Georgia's side."],["Gutzman","Alright, let's take him to report to Harpy, and the bounty of ten thousand will be ours."],["Rena","Georgia..."],["Jon","Georgia."],["Georgia","Our trade is over, you can leave now and take what you want."],["","—She said this and left, clearly having no interest in making things difficult for the two."],["","Rena and Jon exchanged a glance, both unable to hide their euphoria."],["Gutzman","You two."],["Rena","…Gutzman?"],["Jon","Georgia has already agreed to let us go, what do you want?"],["Gutzman","Don't get excited, I didn't mean anything else. I was just thinking, now that you're free, do you have any thoughts about joining a new team?"],["Rena","You wouldn't be here to invite us, would you...?"],["Gutzman","Of course. To be honest, Harpy has provided 'those' arm parts to every mercenary group that took the bounty to capture Douglas."],["Rena","What did you say?!"],["Gutzman","To be honest, you two have already witnessed its power, and you must be aware of how attractive it is to mercenaries... If you continue to fight alone, you might become under fire."],["Rena","I..."],["Jon","No need, thank you for your kindness, Gutzman, but we don't plan to join any team for now."],["Gutzman","......"],["","The two men silently exchanged glances for two seconds, seemingly quickly sharing some unknown information and reaching an agreement."],["","Without gaining Jon's trust, Gutzman didn't mind much. He gave Jon's arm a firm pat."],["Gutzman","...Alright, but if you change your mind in the future, you're always welcome to join us."],["","In the vast no man's land, yellow sand swirls around. On a jeep, Gutzman grips the steering wheel with a spirited demeanor, sweeping away the previous gloom and depression. In the passenger seat, Georgia sits with her arms crossed, resting with her eyes closed."],["","The back seat has been completely removed, and Douglas, hastily bandaged, lies unconscious on a wooden board."],["","There are only three of them in the car. For each other's safety, they have all confirmed before boarding that no one is carrying any weapons or communication devices."],["","The subordinates of both individuals spread out with their STs centered around them, creating a stronger tremor as dozens of STs moved at high speed. If all goes well, they will arrive at the location arranged by Harpy tonight."],["Georgia","I've decided, you can take forty percent of the bounty this time, and we'll split Douglas's men fifty-fifty."],["","Gutzman smiled."],["Gutzman","I thought I'd only get a little helper's fee this time, since you were the one driving the whole operation."],["Georgia","If you think it's unreasonable, I can adjust it down further."],["Gutzman","…Georgia, you know that's not what I meant."],["","Georgia said nothing, focusing on resting with her eyes closed."],["Gutzman","I think we have a good understanding, don't you?"],["Georgia","......"],["Gutzman","The situation isn't good now, going solo is not as good as banding together for warmth. My idea is, if there are suitable jobs coming up, we can continue to cooperate."],["Georgia","That won't be necessary."],["","Georgia said lightly, just three simple words, without any explanation."],["Gutzman","Okay."],["","Gutzman replied with a smile, but his eyes showed no sign of joy."],["","The group quickly arrived at the supply station. They didn't get out of the car, as their underlings took care of refueling."],["Gutzman","I thought you wouldn't let Jon and the others go. After all, they're traitors to the Iguana Mercenary Group—aren't you afraid they'll come for Vendetta later?"],["Georgia","Then we'll handle it when the time comes."],["Gutzman","...You're quite lenient with them, haha, not at all like how harsh you are with me."],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia opened her eyes, with a half-smile."],["Georgia","You also surprised me, Gutzman. You used to work seamlessly with Douglas, even daring to plot my demise together. Now you can shoot him without batting an eye... You're much more ruthless than I am."],["","Gutzman turned his head to look at her, and the two remained silent for several seconds before Gutzman finally laughed."],["Gutzman","Which bastard told you such nonsense? Would anyone really consider me for a big job like 'killing Georgia'? I've only recently made a name for myself; I used to be a lowly person even dogs despised."],["Gutzman","Even if he had such thoughts, he would find someone else, not me."],["Georgia","Don't underestimate yourself. You used to be the second-in-command of the Iguanas, so being an inside man is more than enough. After the job is done, you can split the entire Iguanas among yourselves—Douglas should be quite tempted by this juicy piece, right?"],["","Gutzman's lips froze for a moment, then quickly returned to normal."],["Gutzman","Don't talk nonsense. The Iguanas are just in a rough patch lately, but they used to be untouchable. Kill you? Your subordinates would tear you apart before you even draw your gun."],["Georgia","Heh, the old Iguanas were worth dividing, Gutzman... You know very well that Douglas is only in it for the profit, don't you?"],["Gutzman","......"],["Gutzman","But you're still alive and well, Georgia."],["","No one responded to him anymore."],["","The underling had already refueled, and Gutzman restarted the car, the exhaust pipe spewing thick black smoke as it merged into the vast desert. He looked around, his gaze somewhat nostalgic."],["Gutzman","My grandfather really disliked the desert."],["Gutzman","The desert swallowed up all the nutrients in the soil, and without nutrients, crops couldn't grow. Without crops, there was no income, and the whole family would starve... When I was a child, a few members of our family starved to death."],["Gutzman","But fortunately, my grandfather later planted many trees on that piece of land, gradually nurturing the soil."],["Georgia","I remember you used to run a lumber mill."],["Gutzman","Heh heh heh, yes, thanks to my grandfather's forest."],["Gutzman","Unexpected, right? That forest was considered the family's foundation, and I decided to cut it down."],["Gutzman","But what else can we do? Planting trees is for survival, but can we ever rely solely on planting trees to make a living?"],["Gutzman","My dad doesn't understand these principles; he always believes that the legacy left by our ancestors must be well inherited. But I know very well that if we don't do something, our forest will eventually be burned to ashes by the flames of war."],["Gutzman","Rather than ending up with just ashes, I'd rather cut them down now for some extra money."],["Georgia","......"],["Gutzman","But in the end, I still took the wrong path. When the world is in chaos, whether you're wood or a factory, you're destined to be burned to ashes."],["","Gutzman felt a bit sentimental as he saw Georgia open her eyes, staring blankly at the yellow sand rising outside the window."],["Georgia","You must hold guns and cannons to have the right to control your destiny."],["","She said softly."],["Gutzman","Yes, Georgia, it's always been this way... You truly understand me."],["Gutzman","I've heard some whispers before, saying you're actually a Secret Informer for the military... but I know you're a true mercenary."],["Georgia","What if I really am a soldier of the Defense Force?"],["","Georgia suddenly turned around."],["Gutzman","......"],["Gutzman","That would make me feel quite disgusted."],["","The surroundings quieted down, leaving only the muffled sound of tires rolling over the sand."],["","Zzz—zzz—The vehicle's communicator suddenly emitted intermittent whispers."],["","Georgia's peripheral vision lit up as she saw the firelight falling towards them like meteors from everywhere."],["Georgia Mercenary","Boss! This is bad! The news about us capturing Douglas must have leaked. A lot of people are coming, and we're about to be surrounded!"],["","Georgia almost instantly drew her personal blade, twirling it a few times between her fingers before steadily pressing it against Gutzman's carotid artery."],["Georgia","Turn around! We need to get on the STs."],["Gutzman","Although I know you must have a backup plan, there's no need to reveal your move so quickly—are you suspecting that I'm the one who leaked the information?!"],["Georgia","If you want to clear suspicion, turn now! Otherwise, do you plan to drive this car to your death?"],["","Gutzman gritted his teeth and turned the steering wheel hard to the left, causing the jeep to drift and change direction on the sandy surface."],["","Their STs were positioned toward the middle and rear of the convoy—it would take some time to reach them. But missiles were already raining down from above, detonating around the vehicles and throwing up sand walls three to four meters high."],["","Georgia has already jumped to the back of the carriage, tightly gripping the driver's seat, with the blade in her hand never leaving Gutzman's neck."],["","Gutzman continuously turns the steering wheel, skillfully avoiding bombs. After a few minutes, Georgia finally sees the familiar silhouette of the mech through the swirling sand."],["","With a loud bang, an missile exploded in front of the jeep. Gutzman slammed on the brakes, and Georgia braced herself against the back of the driver's seat to keep her balance. Once the vehicle came to a stop, she immediately opened the trunk, grabbed Douglas, and jumped out."],["","Gutzman quickly followed, and Georgia held onto Douglas without letting go. They were a bit of a distance from the front line, so it was relatively safe."],["Georgia","What should we do with Douglas if we take action? It's not suitable to put him in anyone's ST, so how about..."],["Gutzman Mercenary","On it, Georgia Boss."],["","A henchman of Gutzman ran over from his ST. The moment he spoke, a string in Georgia's mind was plucked lightly."],["Georgia","You... you are..."],["","She suddenly remembered something, and an extremely ominous premonition surged in her heart. As the sandstorm subsided, she instinctively looked at her ST—there should have been Guardians from the Iguana Mercenary Group there to meet her."],["","But beneath Blue Bird's feet, there was no one left. In the sand, only a powerless arm remained uncovered... Her heart suddenly rang with alarm, and she grabbed Douglas and immediately ran towards the jeep."],["","Boom—! Boom boom boom—!"],["","Gutzman fired, hitting Douglas with one shot and blowing out the tires with three more. Even if Georgia gets in the car, she won't be able to drive away. She'll be finished here."],["Gutzman Mercenary","Boss! She's spotted us!"],["Gutzman","Quiet."],["","Gutzman calmly gave the order. He reloaded, spraying the carriage while walking halfway around the car. After a while, there was no movement inside the carriage. Gutzman signaled his subordinates to check the situation."],["","The subordinates cautiously approached and opened the trunk door—"],["","A gust of wind swept by, and Georgia's ghostly figure suddenly appeared. The subordinate only had time to let out a scream before his throat was slit."],["Gutzman","Miscalculated... You're one bullet short of your fate."],["","Georgia tossed the body aside and swiftly drew the gun from his waist, aiming it at Gutzman."],["","She kept adjusting her state with deep breaths - this action caused the blood on her body to continue to slide down. It seems that Gutzman's bullets were not all in vain."],["Georgia","Heh... You chose to drive away with me, seemingly fair, with no room for manipulation... But actually, you had arranged everything long ago."],["Georgia","From the moment I got in the car... This play you've been plotting for so long is finally going to end the way you wanted... You're happy now, aren't you?"],["Gutzman","I'm not that powerful, Georgia. I've always been giving you chances, don't forget."],["Georgia","Stop pretending to be noble. You're just looking for an escape route—after you kill me, the iguanas will hunt you to the ends of the earth."],["Gutzman","Heh."],["","Gutzman changed a magazine."],["Gutzman","I originally prepared two choices for you, but now it seems I was being presumptuous. You won't willingly... become my subordinate, right?"],["Georgia","So, what are the consequences of rejection?"],["Gutzman","Your cause of death will be a stray bullet, killing you instantly. And I, injured while protecting you, will, upon my Awakening, Command the entire Iguana Mercenary Group to seek Vengeance for you."],["Georgia","…What a cliché script."],["Gutzman","Is that so? Sorry for the lack of culture. Back then, besides fighting for the Iguana with you, I should have read more books."],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia suddenly throws the gun in her hand to Gutzman and slowly raises her two hands."],["Gutzman","You change..."],["Georgia","Want to hear the third ending I wrote for you?"],["Georgia","Just let me go. I won't ask the iguana for help, but instead enter this uninhabited area behind me—"],["Georgia","No water, no food, no guns, no medicine, just me with four gunshot wounds—if you think scratches aren't enough, you can shoot me a few more times."],["","Gutzman furrowed his brow."],["Georgia","If you really kill me, my subordinates won't believe the nonsense that \"Georgia was killed by a stray bullet.\" They would rather mistakenly kill you than let you go."],["Georgia","But if I go missing in this battle... without a body, they can only suspect, not conclude. You'll have plenty of time to wash the iguana into whatever you want... How about it?"],["","Gutzman was silent for a moment, then took out the magazine of the gun Georgia had just thrown to him, confirmed there was only one bullet left inside, and tossed it back."],["","He wanted to say something, but as he opened his mouth, his vocal cords suddenly tightened, like a jammed gun."],["","He had known this woman for many years and had spoken tens of thousands of words. Ideals, desires, hatred... everything that needed to be said had been said. Yet, in this last moment of farewell, he still felt as if he hadn't said enough. The words he wanted to say were stuck in his throat, unable to utter a single word."],["","But it doesn't matter, Georgia had long known about the past he had been planning, and she understood that he was a complete betrayer. His words would no longer be heeded."],["Gutzman","Your art of language will always be remembered by me... Georgia, just turn your back and keep... keep moving forward."],["Georgia","You should've died sooner, Gutzman... Let me return this bullet to you personally."],["","Georgia hides in the shadow of the rock, remaining motionless, with only a slight rise and fall in her chest."],["","Her scrapes had been hastily bound with torn strips of cloth, but the long trek had rendered such crude bandaging useless. Blood ran down her limbs, leaving dark stains in her wake wherever she passed."],["","Twenty minutes ago, her limbs had already started to go numb, forcing her to make the choice to stay here and recover her strength."],["","The surroundings were silent, with only the whispering wind passing by. Was she the only one left in the World? Georgia stared blankly at the dim sky, belatedly realizing the chill throughout her body."],["","\"You must keep walking, walk out of this desert, Georgia.\""],["","No, I have no feet."],["","\"Then crawl forward... You can't just wait here to die, Georgia.\""],["","No... I don't have hands either."],["","\"...\""],["","\"Then what is the point of making this choice?\""],["","Her cracked lips moved for a second."],["Georgia","I don't want..."],["","\"But you're about to die.\""],["Georgia","......"],["","In that moment, she felt all the fluids in her body flowing, rushing to her nasal cavity, rushing to her tear glands, rushing to her unhealed wounds."],["","The intense stimulation washed over her long-dried and solidified thoughts, setting all her ideas in motion, never before so clear, active, and soaring."],["Georgia","Do you think… my mission… can finally come to an end?"],["","\"What mission do you bear?\""],["Georgia","......"],["Georgia","I... I am the shadow of the Defense Force... The Defense Force... needs me... to keep moving... in the darkness..."],["","\"...\""],["","You're wrong, Georgia."],["","It's me, it's me who needs you, I need you to live well."],["","Ge... Gerard?"],["Officer","Georgia, don't die, wake up... Georgia! Georgia! Georgia—!"],["","Georgia suddenly opened her eyes, gasping for air like someone rescued from drowning. She looked around in confusion, finding nothing around her."],["","She trembles as she extends her two hands, pale red blood tears dripping into her palms, pooling briefly before slipping through her fingers."],["","She dreamed again... Just now... She dreamed of her officer again."],["","Yes... sir... sir...! There's still a way, she still has a way!"],["","Georgia struggled to tear the cloth from her arm, looked at the wound on her arm, gritted her teeth and tore it open, then extended her fingers to pull out a small chip from deep within the wound."],["","This is a signal transmitter, implanted in her arm by the officer on the day she left the Defense Force. No matter where she is, headquarters can receive the location information emitted by this little device."],["","This is her last hope."],["Georgia","Sir... please..."],["","She activated the transmitter, and the green signal light lit up. The signal light did not blink, indicating that her signal was not acknowledged by headquarters."],["","The green glow was like a guiding light to the underworld, persistently welcoming her."],["","...Still not working?"],["","She slowly leaned against the rock and looked at the dim sky again. The sky was getting darker, and the temperature was dropping. The vitality that had burst from her body seemed like a fleeting moment... making her feel like she had become a rock."],["","......"],["","......"],["","Ah..."],["","She hasn't said goodbye yet."]],"468317101":[["Jon","Dinner's ready—why is there only one light on? It's so dark here."],["","Jon carries a stack of food boxes as he enters, thumping down the stairs. Although the lighting is not sufficient, fortunately, he has become accustomed to the structure of this basement over the past few days, rarely missing a step."],["Rena","No problem, I just need the visibility in the work area to meet clear standards."],["","Rena is hunched over the desk, tinkering with something, and doesn't turn around when she hears Jon's voice."],["Jon","Come over and have some food."],["Rena","Alright—wow, so much? Did you empty the supermarket?"],["Jon","It's a complete mess outside right now. To be safe, we should lay low for the time being, especially since we still have that hot potato on our hands."],["Rena","What happened?"],["Jon","It's Gutzman. That guy has been causing quite a stir lately."],["Jon","He claimed Harpy's bounty, and many people were furious, threatening to teach this newcomer a lesson. But their words came too late; Gutzman had already challenged the leader of the Shadows, Malcolm."],["Rena","Ma-Malcolm? I remember he was quite formidable. Back when we were with the Iguanas, even Georgia had to be cautious when facing him..."],["Jon","Yes, but times change."],["Rena","Gutzman won?"],["Jon","He won. With so much capital at his disposal, what can't he buy? People, equipment, mechs, he has it all. How can Malcolm keep up?"],["Jon","Right now, other mercenary groups are either discussing banding together to dampen Gutzman's momentum or keeping a low profile to avoid getting involved—we shouldn't join the commotion either. It's just as well that your research has reached a critical stage, so it's better to keep a low profile."],["Rena","...Jon, what if I have to take on some work..."],["Jon","Huh?"],["Rena","In fact... my experiment consumables are almost used up, and purchasing another batch would be quite an expense... Uh, I've posted a recruitment task on Skynet, so maybe someone will contact me soon."],["Jon","Hmm..."],["Rena","I did all this before you told me these things, and at that time, I didn't know things would develop like this..."],["Jon","Haha, don't worry, Rena. I don't mean to stop or blame you. Since there's no other way, we'll just have to be cautious. I can help out when the time comes."],["Rena","...Sigh, if, if we were still with the Iguanas now..."],["","At this point, the two fell silent simultaneously."],["Jon","Georgia may be cold, but she's definitely a good boss—as long as you're recognized as part of the Iguanas."],["Rena","Speaking of which, you haven't mentioned her at all. Shouldn't she be splitting the bounty with Gutzman?"],["Jon","It's not that I don't want to talk about her, but I haven't heard any news about her. It's strange; she seems to have disappeared after we parted ways."],["Rena","Could something have happened—"],["","Beep—several beeps interrupted their conversation."],["Rena","Hmm? It's a message from Skynet... My recruitment task has a reply!"],["Jon","What did the employer say?"],["Rena","The employer said... it's a small job. He only wants one person's life, but didn't say who. I'm supposed to go to a place tomorrow, and someone will meet me there."],["Rena","He also said... I can check out the situation first and then decide whether to take the job."],["Jon","Should we go? The mission details are a bit too blur..."],["Rena","But the commission is really... well, let's go check it out. If things seem off, we can bail immediately!"],["Rena","We've arrived at mission coordinates EW02. What do we do next?"],["Electronic Voice","Just a moment."],["","In the communicator, the employer's voice is just a processed electronic sound, indistinguishable between male and female."],["","Jon and Rena exchanged a glance and began checking their gun magazines. This was their first meeting with the employer, and until they were sure the employer posed no threat, a certain level of self-protection was necessary."],["","The meeting place with the employer was a wilderness area, with the nearest man-made structure being an abandoned ST repair factory. EW02 was in a hollow behind a boulder, and dressed in pretense suits, they blended almost perfectly into the environment."],["Rena","Dressed like this, do you think the employer will recognize us?"],["Jon","He hadn't seen them before, so he probably doesn't recognize people by their faces."],["Georgia Mercenary","You're here—"],["","Suddenly, a female voice comes from above, and the two instinctively point their guns at the source, only to reveal surprised expressions the next moment."],["Rena","Why is it you? You're the employer? Aren't you Georgia's subordinate? Georgia, she—"],["Georgia Mercenary","With you all here, everyone is present."],["Georgia Mercenary","The target will appear soon, and I'll brief you on the operation."],["Rena","W-Wait a minute—we haven't accepted the job yet!"],["Georgia Mercenary","Heh, come up and see for yourselves, you'll agree soon enough."],["","Is there such a thing? Rena climbed up the rock in confusion."],["","A convoy of off-road vehicles approached from afar, passed under the rock where they were hiding, and sped ahead."],["","The convoy stopped in the field, and a person got out of the leading car. Jon raised his tactical binoculars, and a familiar figure appeared in his view."],["Jon","Gutzman? You want to kill Gutzman?!"],["Georgia Mercenary","He deserves to die for daring to attack Georgia... He won't be missed—"],["Rena","What?! Georgia... she's dead?!"],["Georgia Mercenary","She's missing. We were attacked on the way to report to Harpy. The boss was in a car with Douglas and Gutzman. After we dealt with the enemy and went back to find them, only Gutzman and Douglas were left at the scene!"],["Georgia Mercenary","Douglas took several shots and was barely clinging to life. Gutzman was badly wounded too. But our boss—somehow—just vanished without a trace!"],["Georgia Mercenary","When Gutzman woke up, he said they encountered another group at the time, and the boss might have been taken away by them... I don't believe it!"],["Georgia Mercenary","Gutzman must have done something, something must have happened between him and Georgia... I'm going to catch him and get to the bottom of it. If he really hurt the boss, I'll make him wish he were dead!"],["Jon","......"],["Rena","......"],["Jon","Now Gutzman's forces are strong, and most people won't easily provoke him. How confident are you?"],["Georgia Mercenary","Our people have already infiltrated his team. At that time, he put on a tearful act, saying he wanted to avenge the boss, so we joined his team and waited for a chance to take action against him."],["Georgia Mercenary","He has arranged for an Obsidian Hades, and today he's coming to pick it up himself. We'll shoot down the transport plane first, and chaos will ensue at the scene. Our people will use tranquilizer darts to knock him out, creating the illusion that he was shot."],["Georgia Mercenary","With no leader, that's when we take action."],["","She didn't directly answer Jon's question. Perhaps she understood that this operation was very risky, but they had reasons they couldn't ignore."],["Jon","...I acknowledge Georgia as the leader, and since this has happened to her... I'm willing to help you capture Gutzman."],["Rena","...Jon?"],["Georgia Mercenary","What about you? Now that you know our entire plan of action, it's impossible for you to just leave."],["","Jon shields Rena behind him."],["Jon","You've only recruited one person, and since I've taken that spot, then Rena—"],["Rena","It's okay, Jon. I can help too, although I might not be able to do much, but for such a dangerous mission, you..."],["Georgia Mercenary","Your choice is correct. Taking out Gutzman benefits you as well. Don't forget those things in your hands. Now that the boss is gone, Gutzman has every reason to unite with Harpy against you."],["Georgia Mercenary","Rather than waiting to be threatened by Gutzman in the future, it's better to take the initiative and completely nip the disaster in the bud. Alright, time is running out. It's time to show Gutzman what blood for blood means..."],["Rena","Hello? I have arrived at the designated location, awaiting the start of the operation."],["Jon","Understood, I've also reached the designated location. Watch for the mole's signal."],["Rena","Understood, I'll support him in time."],["","Jon quietly lifted the straw hat used for pretense, extending the tactical binoculars slightly to look into the distance. In the lens, Gutzman had already returned to the car, surrounded tightly by his subordinates, protected so well that not even a fly could get in."],["Rena","Hades... Have you ever seen Hades, Jon?"],["Jon","I've heard people say it's unimaginably expensive."],["Rena","Yeah... Haha, driving that kind of ST must be every mercenary's dream, right? If this mission succeeds, I wonder if I can apply to study it..."],["Jon","...Rena."],["Rena","Yes?"],["Jon","Actually, you don't have to agree to join this operation... You should know that the iguanas are just making a desperate gamble."],["Rena","I know, I'm not stupid."],["Jon","And you still agreed?"],["Rena","Didn't you agree too?"],["Jon","...Sigh, the mercenary group I once served has fallen to this point, I can't just stand by."],["Rena","...I'm not a fool, and I'm not heartless either."],["Rena","Georgia may always seem fierce... but initially, she was the one who gave me my first lab bench. She said the things I made were useful and told me not to waste my talent."],["Jon","Yeah... initially... initially, she was the one who brought everyone together, and that's how we got the Iguana."],["","Jon murmured. Suddenly, a shadow appeared in his lens, and the engine's loud roar echoed into their communication channel."],["Rena","So, let's do this job well, just for... for the fierce Georgia."],["Jon","For the fierce Georgia—attention, Rena, I see the transport aircraft."],["","The transport aircraft slowly approached Gutzman's convoy, and the shadow in the clouds grew larger. Jon glanced down at his watch, and as the second hand clicked to the number 12, a bright burst of fire suddenly erupted on the horizon."],["","Three rockets fired in rapid succession, streaking skyward and carving through the air like blades, black smoke trailing behind them."],["","Boom———!! The transport aircraft is hit, losing its balance and starting to spin in the air, soon to crash."],["","Jon quickly aimed his tactical binoculars in Gutzman's direction, feeling tense. He didn't know how the Iguana people would act. Could he really kill Gutzman in front of everyone?"],["","Gutzman has already gotten out of the car. Jon is uncertain, thinking they should quickly drive away from the crash site. Gutzman got out of the car, how can two legs outrun gravity? Unconsciously, Jon feels his palms getting a bit clammy."],["","He watches Gutzman stride forward, when suddenly a figure leaps out of the car, pouncing towards Gutzman like a leopard. The gun in his hand flashes twice, and Gutzman instantly falls forward, rolling over several times."],["","Jon was both surprised and delighted to find that the iguana's mole had successfully infiltrated Gutzman's side and completed the most crucial step of the plan!"],["","With this, they might actually be able to pull off this job."],["Jon","Rena! Prepare for action! It's our turn to take the stage!"],["Rena","Understood! I saw the signal flare he launched, I'm heading there now—zzzz—zzzzzz—"],["","Static crackled into the comms channel—familiar somehow—but Jon didn't pay it any mind. What came next would be their real fight."],["","He stowed the binoculars and rubbed his hands together. A sudden gust lifted the straw hat he was using for camouflage, and he instinctively reached up to hold it down."],["","—The tense assassination moments ago had left him slick with sweat. A cool breeze should have eased the heat, but with the straw hat gone from his head, the expected chill never came…?"],["","...Where's his straw hat? Jon was stunned. His straw hat was blown away by the wind... but it didn't fall to the ground."],["","Buzz—buzz—he heard that burst of static again, as if it were right beside his ear… What was making that sound? It was so familiar, like something he heard every single day."],["","He instinctively turned around—first saw his straw hat—gently pinched between two wide, sturdy mechanical fingers—just like he would pick up a grain of rice that had fallen to the ground."],["","Jon slowly widened his eyes—aside from maintaining STs, he had never been this close to one, close enough to see the peeling yellow paint on its shell, close enough to smell the lubricant on it, close enough to—"],["","Close enough to notice the rotating lens in its electronic eye, making one feel as if they were gazing into the eyes of a living creature."],["","Zzz—zzz—the ST in front of him moved again, placing the straw hat back on Jon's head, but unfortunately, it ended up crooked."],["","Didn't expect it to be you... Jon."],["","Jon was dumbfounded, he knew this voice... he knew... he recognized—!"],["","No, no—! Everyone must know! The operation must be terminated! Terminate it now—!!!"],["Jon","Substitute!! The one who died was a substitute!! Terminate the operation!! Terminate it now—!!!!!!"],["","He roared with such intensity that his voice seemed to tear apart, and the last few words were only mouthed without sound due to his stiff vocal cords."],["Gutzman","Hahaha, why terminate? Jon, I've been waiting for this moment for a long time. You are the alchemical stones delivered to my doorstep, and I couldn't be happier—"],["","All the blood in Jon's body seemed to rush to his hands as he emptied the entire magazine at Gillesrais with the fastest speed of his life, scrambling out of cover."],["","Gutzman's laughter still lingered hauntingly behind him, and Jon could only run for his life, faster... faster...! Run——!"],["","Trap! It's all a trap! Gutzman saw through everything the Iguana had planned and turned it against them to catch them all in one fell swoop!"],["","After he moved here, he didn't feel a hint of vibration from the approaching mech... It's Gutzman, he's always been... he's always been there!!"],["","Jon shouted loudly, venting the displeasure of being fooled. A burst of dirt exploded at his feet, Gutzman had already fired, and he moved his hands and feet more quickly, dodging the ballistics with erratic turns."],["","Boom, boom... boom, boom, boom... The sound of intense artillery fire gradually rises all around. The battle has begun, and the swirling dust clouds Jon's mind like a looming shadow."],["","An ST… He had to get into his ST right now—once the fighting spread, he'd be nothing more than a crushed lump of flesh underfoot."],["","But his ST was parked behind Gutzman… Jon ran while glancing back. Gillesrais's silhouette was already blurred, yet the muzzle flash was still glaringly clear—there was no turning back now. He had to rendezvous with the Iguana, fast!"],["","Bang bang bang bang! Another burst of fierce gunfire rang out. Jon gritted his teeth and charged forward, suddenly seeing a familiar silhouette appear at the far end of the swirling dust. It stood there steadily, with a proud posture, holding two swords like a silent warrior."],["Jon","...Rena?"],["Jon","No, no! Rena! Can you hear my voice? Rena! Gutzman is not dead! Gutzman is behind me! Don't go over there! Let's regroup with the Iguana first—!"],["","Jon seems to hear the sizzling sound again—Rex moves, slowly lowering its center of gravity, preparing for an impact. The dual blades in its hands switch to a reverse one-handed grip, their tips reflecting a chilling gleam under the firelight."],["Jon","Rena—! Stop—!"],["","Rex's electronic eye flared with a blinding red cross—fully charged. Jon's heart shot up into his throat. He yelled, but the sound was instantly swallowed by the shriek of Rex powering up."],["","The massive ST kicked up a gale-force shockwave. Jon hunched over, shielding himself as sand and grit slammed into him. War-drum tremors pounded up through the ground beneath his feet—Rex was closing in fast—"],["","He instinctively looks up at a certain moment and sees an ST as big as a mountain speeding over his head, disappearing from sight in the blink of an eye."],["Jon","No... Rena..."],["","He reflexively runs in Rex's direction."],["","Bzz—bzz—"],["","—hear—bzz—can you hear—bzz—Jon! If you can hear me, respond! Jon!"],["Jon","Rena? Rena?! Is that you?! Where are you?! It's Gutzman! Come back -"],["Rena","I'm heading your way—bzz—Give me—bzz—specific coordinates—bzz—damn communication signal—bzz—"],["Jon","What?! Isn't that you in Rex? Then who is it? Who's piloting your ST?"],["Rena","It's—bzz—her—bzz—"],["","Jon didn't hear anything, but he had an unbelievable suspicion in his heart. If this suspicion is true, then..."],["","His consciousness gradually diffuses, seemingly chasing the bursting Rex along the rugged terrain—at this moment, Gillesrais is changing the magazine, and the smoke in front of it suddenly expands into a half-sphere, followed by a blade that cuts through the sphere!"],["Gutzman","What?!"],["","Gutzman, stunned, raises his shield, the blade clashing against the steel shield with dazzling sparks. The two massive STs wrestle against each other like colliding continents."],["Gutzman","Rex? Are you Rena? So you came too? Heh... Even though you're no longer with the Iguana Mercenary Group, you're still here to avenge Georgia. Such deep feelings and loyalty."],["","Clang! Clang clang clang clang clang—! The silent warrior remains speechless, its blade continuously striking Gillesrais's steel shield. The blade's shadow remnant, each cut precisely overlaps at one spot, and the sparks flying off scorch the ground into blackened circles."],["","With the final strike, the samurai leans back, charging with the tip of the blade aimed at the sole opening, and thrusts it in with the presence of a mountain pressing down!"],["Gutzman","What is that?!"],["","Gutzman throws away the steel shield and immediately retreats, feeling a lingering fear because Rex's blade tip almost pierced Gillesrais's pilot cabin!"],["","This guy isn't Rena! He's fought her before—there's no way that little brat ever carried pressure like this!"],["","It... it feels more like... more like—Gutzman's throat rolled as he tried to suppress the thoughts that had already boiled over in his mind. Impossible, impossible!"],["","That woman has already been consumed by the desert! Turned into sand and will never return!"],["","Rex pulled the blade from the steel shield, \"looked\" at the already curled edge, and then discarded it without hesitation."],["","It once again holds the knife with both hands, assuming a standard Strong Attack stance, and slowly lowers its center of gravity—"],["Gutzman","Who are you? Mayer? Rosie? Castilla?! Speak! Who are you really?!"],["","Gutzman..."],["","A hoarse voice came from Rex, evoking his distant memories... In the endless sand, a few firestones suddenly rolled out, scorching his nerves with sharp pain."],["Gutzman","Geo—Georgia—"],["Georgia","I am \"Wildfire,\" Gutzman, back from Hell, burning through."],["Gutzman","Georgia———!!!"],["","Gillesrais angrily pulls the Trigger—empty! His magazine!! Gutzman's heart tightens, Georgia's sudden appearance had shocked him too much, he hadn't had time to change the magazine—"],["","Rex's shadow suddenly appears like a ghost! Gutzman instinctively retreats—but it's too late, Rex's blade is already storming down—boom!!"],["","Gillesrais suddenly twists to the right, and Rex's blade swiftly cuts off his L-Arm!"],["","Gutzman quickly adjusted the controls, maneuvering Gillesrais to charge madly into the smoke and dust—he was going to find his last trump card... Hades! As long as he had that Invincible ST—as long as he had Hades—Georgia would surely—!"],["","Rex did not chase after him. It dropped the last knife in its hand and resumed standing tall in silence."],["","Half a minute later, a voice every Iguana member knew all too well echoed through the comm channel—"],["Georgia","This is Georgia, all Iguanas members now follow my command."],["Georgia","Kill Gutzman."]],"468317301":[["","Hades fell helplessly from mid-air, its heavy body creating a significant dent in the ground."],["","The violent tremor briefly stunned Gutzman, but the ST's built-in alarm signal quickly brought his consciousness back."],["","Gutzman quickly adjusted the control stick, maneuvering Gillesrais to charge madly into the smoke and dust—he was going to find his last trump card... Hades! As long as he had that Invincible ST—as long as he had Hades—Georgia would surely—!"],["","Seeing Rex's blade about to strike Hades' pilot cabin, Gutzman quickly grabs the ST beside him and throws it at Rex's blade."],["Georgia","Gutzman—you despicable scoundrel!"],["","Rex quickly sheathed his sword and sidestepped to avoid the ST, while Gutzman was already maneuvering Hades to rapidly retreat."],["","Seeing that he was about to escape, Rex's electronic eye swiftly aimed at Hades' legs and hurled a long sword with all his might—"],["","Clang! Got it!"],["Gutzman","Damn! Damn! Damn Georgia——!"],["","Clang——! Just as Hades drew the knife from the leg joint, Rex's attack was already descending from above, forcing Gutzman to block the slash with the knife in his hand, or he would have been cut in half."],["Gutzman","Not finishing you off with a shot that day was the worst decision I've ever made, Georgia——"],["Georgia","Too bad you won't get another chance, maybe this is your fate!"],["","The two clashed again, their blades sparking countless flames."],["Gutzman","No... Georgia! My fate was sealed by my own hands in the Northwest Jungle! I cut down the forest left by my ancestors, I made the choice to join this world, I chose to become a mercenary! I'm no longer that incompetent Forest Ranger!"],["Gutzman","Power, status, wealth! I sacrificed so much to have everything I have now, how could I let you take them away so easily—!"],["","Scalding black smoke burst from Hades's joints as its energy-overloaded arm slammed down on Rex in a berserk strike, instantly severing the blade in its grasp and driving straight toward Giorgia's position."],["Rena","Stay alert—!"],["","Two missiles came screaming in fast. Gutzman yanked Hades into a rapid retreat while firing several missiles skyward. The trajectories collided in a thunderous explosion, scattering countless burning fragments through the air."],["","Rex raised his arm to shield for a few seconds, but Hades took the opportunity to flee to the distance."],["Georgia","Trying to escape?"],["","Georgia quickly pulled the control stick to chase after, and the two STs soon disappeared like meteors into the horizon."],["Rena","Quick! Let's catch up!"],["","Georgia races along the tracks on the ground, spotting an abandoned ST repair shop in the distance. The shop isn't large, but it's piled high with miscellaneous scrap metal."],["","Rex slowly drove through the gate, and the traces of Hades' movements had already extended deep inside."],["Georgia","It's useless to keep running, Gutzman. Why don't you come out and we can talk——"],["","Rex moved slowly, its electronic eye rotating at high frequency, constantly analyzing factors in the environment that might threaten its change."],["Georgia","I know you don't trust me, but you have to face the reality of failure."],["Georgia","If you come out now, I'll give you a chance to negotiate——whether you seize it and try to persuade me to spare you, or live like a street rat in hiding, it's your choice."],["","No one answered her."],["","The road was almost at its end—this was the last stretch where Gutzman could set an ambush for her."],["","Rex holds the twin blades in both forward and reverse grips, allowing it to cover attacks from every direction. It suddenly stops because the soil in front of it has clearly changed color, indicating that it might have been disturbed."],["","There might be landmines buried beneath this layer of soil... Georgia ponders and decides to take a detour."],["","Rex circled around and cut open the path blocked by piles of scrap metal with a knife—beep beep beep beep—beneath layers of scrap metal, the red warning lights on the bomb flashed continuously!"],["","—No time—boom!!! The soaring flame blasted a huge hole in the repair shop."],["Jon","Not good, Georgia might be ambushed! Let's hurry over!"],["","Jon and Rena led Iguana at full speed toward the blast site, their mechs charging straight into the flames. Rex was already down, charred black from head to toe, sparks flickering across its hull."],["Rena","No sign of Hades. Could he have escaped again?"],["Georgia Mercenary","Boss! Boss, are you okay?!"],["","Georgia's subordinates quickly dragged Rex out and forcibly pried open the cockpit. Georgia had some bloodstains on her, but fortunately, she remained conscious."],["Georgia","Go... go after Gutzman. He can't have gone far. Watch for ground traces..."],["Georgia Mercenary","I know, I know, boss. I'll send someone right away—"],["Jon","I'll go with you. Leave more people here to watch over the boss, in case Gutzman has any tricks up his sleeve."],["","After Jon finished speaking, unexpectedly, no one immediately agreed with him—he was no longer a member of the Iguana, and joining their operation required the boss's permission."],["","Georgia closed her eyes for a moment, pausing for a few seconds before speaking."],["Georgia","Go ahead, don't forget, Gutzman isn't dead yet. Your job isn't over yet."],["Jon","I know—Rena, you stay here, we'll be back soon."],["Rena","Sigh—"],["","Without waiting for Rena's reply, Jon led the rest of Iguana away at speed. The remaining members didn't waste a second—quickly assigning watch positions and carrying Georgia out to tend to her wounds."],["","Rena hesitated in the pilot cabin, unsure whether to go down and do something. Although Georgia didn't trouble them when she and Jon left the Iguana Mercenary Group, it was an undeniable fact that they chose to find another way out during the group's most difficult time."],["","What does Georgia think? Shouldn't she avoid getting in the way... But just now, Georgia had so many STs to choose from, yet she borrowed Rex from her. Maybe she doesn't really dislike her that much? Rena's mind was in a mess."],["Georgia","If Gutzman doesn't die in the end this time, I'll deduct 20% from your commission—it's standard practice."],["Rena","Got it."],["Georgia","But I heard that my people did not fully inform you of the task details before accepting the mission. According to the usual practice, you can request corresponding compensation."],["Rena","...How much compensation?"],["Georgia","20%."],["Rena","...Well, can you compensate me?"],["Georgia","Okay."],["Rena","...Thank you, Georgia."],["","Rena sighed, her mind even more confused. After a while, she mustered up the courage to ask a question she was very curious about."],["Rena","Georgia, what exactly happened between you and Gutzman after we parted ways?"],["Georgia","...Nothing, he wanted to kill me, and I ran away."],["Georgia Mercenary","But we searched that area for a long time and couldn't find you. Boss, where did you go?"],["Georgia","......"],["","Georgia was silent for a long time, and finally just shook her head."],["Georgia","I'm tired and need to rest for a while. Wake me up as soon as they have any news, got it?"],["Georgia Mercenary","Alright, boss, you can sleep soundly. I'll stay here and watch over you."],["","Georgia immediately closed her eyes. She originally just wanted to rest for a while and avoid answering those inconvenient questions, but perhaps her body had indeed reached its limit."],["","Shortly after closing her eyes, she truly fell into a deep sleep."],["","Beep-boop—That's the sound of Spark cracking."],["","Georgia's consciousness is hazy, and she vaguely feels a hint of warmth, gradually restoring sensation to her stiff limbs."],["","The wounds on her body still hurt a lot, but a strange coolness gently envelops them, making the pain not so unbearable."],["","—Her forehead suddenly feels cool; someone must have taken away the cloth originally placed there to cool her down and replaced it with a new one. She might have a fever."],["","...Wait."],["","Now that you're awake, have something to eat. You need some nutritions."],["","That voice is... is... is...!"],["Georgia","...Sir."],["","She struggled to regain consciousness from the chaos, slowly opening her eyes—a familiar silhouette sat in front of the fire... It was indeed him, not an illusion."],["Officer","Drink some water first, sip it slowly."],["","The officer handed her a water bottle, thoughtfully equipped with a straw."],["Georgia","...Sir, it really is you."],["Officer","It's me. Sorry, Georgia, East Milkhama was in chaos recently, and I ran into some trouble, so I couldn't respond to your messages in time."],["Georgia","I know, it's okay. It's good that everything's fine now."],["Officer","...Fine? How did you end up like this?"],["Officer","When I rushed over, you were barely breathing. Luckily, I was nearby; if I had been any later, I would have been here to collect your body!"],["","Georgia silently takes a few sips of water, her head down as she traces the texture of the water bottle in her hand."],["Georgia","It's okay, none of that happened, and I got my life back."],["Officer","......"],["","The officer sighs, tossing aside the fire poker, and looks up at the cloud-covered sky. It's evening, and soon the sky will be filled with stars."],["","Even though it's the same world, the land is filled with smoke, yet the sky, whether day or night, has its own splendor."],["Officer","How long has it been, Georgia?"],["Georgia","…I have a bad memory, I forgot."],["","The question was vague, but Georgia understood what he meant."],["Officer","Haha, it's fine, these things aren't worth remembering…"],["Georgia","......"],["Officer","......"],["Officer","Leave here, Georgia."],["Georgia","...What?"],["Officer","Leave Milkhama, it's about to erupt in warfire—unlike those minor skirmishes before, there's nothing you or I can do anymore."],["Georgia","What about you, sir? Are you leaving too?"],["Officer","No, I am a member of the DLAF and will fight to the last moment following the code."],["Georgia","......"],["Georgia","Me too. I am also a member of the DLAF, I..."],["","The officer suddenly turned to look at Georgia. He had been sitting with his back turned, and Georgia hadn't noticed anything unusual. But now, as they made eye contact, she realized half of the officer's face was wrapped in bandages."],["Georgia","—! Your, your eyes!"],["","Gerard is the finest Sniper—but now one of his proud eyes is covered by a blood-stained bandage."],["Officer","It's nothing, just couldn't escape the ST in time during the last battle... got injured in the explosion."],["Georgia","The eyeball is such a precisely constructed part, even the slightest damage—!"],["","In her excitement, Georgia's tone couldn't help but rise, but Gerard just looked at her calmly."],["","He knew the condition of his body better than Georgia did, but he had already calmly accepted the realistic situation."],["Georgia","...Sorry."],["Officer","Yesterday, I woke up in the hospital, surrounded by painful groans."],["Officer","Some lost their hands, some lost their legs, some lost vital organs, and some are waiting for death... In that battle, I only lost an eye. Georgia, I've been very fortunate."],["","Georgia lowered her head and exhaled a deep, scorching breath."],["Officer","Let's go, Georgia."],["Officer","This war didn't start because of us, nor will it end because of us, but many will perish because of it... I'm sorry, I thought we could change something."],["","Georgia felt at a loss. She had never seen Gerard so utterly dispirited—like a diamond that once shone brilliantly, now scorched by searing heat into a lump of ash."],["","If nothing is said, he might just be blown away by the night wind."],["Georgia","...Then if you continue to stay here, you'll be killed sooner or later."],["Officer","It's okay, it's my responsibility. If the defense force still needs me, I'll fight until the last moment—but you're different, Georgia."],["Officer","You don't have to bear this responsibility. As long as you make up your mind, I can help you start over in a safer place."],["Georgia","......"],["Officer","The change you are hoping for may be difficult to come... But don't be afraid, you still have a way out."],["Georgia","A safer place... Will Rosie and Castilla be there?"],["Officer","You can take them with you."],["Georgia","Will Nora be there?"],["Officer","As long as you remember Nora, she will always be by your side."],["Georgia","Will you be there?"],["Officer","......"],["","Gerard's face trembled slightly."],["Georgia","...I knew from a young age that many things cannot be changed by human effort, sir."],["Georgia","I don't like rain, don't like hunger, don't like blood, don't like all the inhumane villains in this world, don't like... In short, there are many, many more."],["Georgia","But I've lived until now, and I've only managed to eliminate a tiny bit of them from my life."],["Georgia","Changing one's life is so difficult... let alone changing the world."],["Officer","...This is different, Georgia."],["Georgia","In my eyes, it's no different from what you said. If it's hard to change, then it's hard to change, I get it."],["Officer","What's that supposed to mean?"],["Georgia","I've accepted this reality."],["Officer","But this goes against your original intention. Haven't you always wanted to strive to change this reality? For this ideal, you risked your life time and time again!"],["Officer","Now you're just betting your life on an impossible vision, what's the point of all this?!"],["Georgia","I'm protecting the people I care about, I'm safeguarding their will!"],["Officer","......"],["","The air suddenly calmed down, and for a moment, only the crackling sound of sparks could be heard."],["Georgia","...I don't have many friends, I cherish them, sir."],["Georgia","Over the years, I know you've secretly helped me a lot... Few people consider me, and I also want to... do my best."],["Officer","I don't need you..."],["Georgia","This is also for Nora. You are her only brother, and I can't be indifferent to your life or death, sir."],["Officer","I'll pass..."],["Georgia","If one day I die... I hope to die on this land with all of you."],["","Gerard opened his mouth, still wanting to persuade her, but the woman before him looked at him with eyes full of steadiness. The candlelight made her face almost transparent, yet Gerard saw a radiant light in her eyes."],["","She's always been a stubborn woman, determined to do whatever she wants, no matter how difficult or challenging."],["Officer","...Sigh, none of them listen... When Nora decided to join the defense force, she said the same thing to you..."],["Officer","\"Brother... I hope to always be by your side.\" Now she truly rests here."],["Georgia","...I will live well."],["","In the crevices of this world, living earnestly."],["Officer","Is that so?"],["","Gerard looked up at the sky again."],["Officer","Georgia, don't forget this, don't forget what you said to me today..."],["Georgia Mercenary","Shh... Keep it down, the boss isn't awake yet."],["","Jon paused, then tiptoed closer. Georgia was indeed still asleep, facing inward, her breathing calm."],["Jon","We followed the trail, but only found an empty shell of Hades. Gutzman has already fled, and no footprints were found nearby."],["Rena","How is that possible? How did he escape without leaving footprints?"],["Georgia Mercenary","Shh! I told you to keep it down! What if you wake the boss?!"],["Rena","Uh... Sorry..."],["Georgia Mercenary","Tsk! Damn Gutzman, he actually got away..."],["Georgia","What are you talking about?"],["Georgia Mercenary","B-Boss! You're awake!"],["Georgia","Jon? You're back, Gutz... huh, let him get away, right."],["","Jon looks apologetic, Georgia knows in her heart, the operation must have failed."],["Georgia","Since things have come to this, let's retreat quickly and focus on counting Gutzman's assets."],["Georgia Mercenary","Yeah! He's been in the spotlight quite a bit lately. If we take down his hideout, it'll definitely be a big payday!"],["","Under Georgia's command, the entire iguana team began to retreat in an orderly manner."],["","Due to her injuries, Georgia didn't pilot the ST but was driven back by her subordinates."],["Georgia Mercenary","Boss, Jon and the others are catching up too. Should we drive them away?"],["Georgia","…No, let them follow."],["Georgia Mercenary","…Hey, Boss, have you forgiven them?"],["Georgia","Just drive."],["Georgia Mercenary","Oh..."],["","Georgia glanced at the rearview mirror where Dias was half-dragging, half-carrying Rex, quickly looked away, and closed her eyes again."],["","As the sun sets, the mighty ST convoy drives into the endless night."],["","That unforeseeable future remained silent, but Georgia knew that, at the very end of this night, dawnlight would spill across the horizon."]]};
